1
00:00:00,668 --> 00:00:03,303
♪ IN THE NOT
TOO DISTANT FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,607
♪ SOMEWHERE IN TIME AND SPACE ♪

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,743
♪ LIKE NELSON
AND HIS ROBOT PALS ♪

4
00:00:09,777 --> 00:00:12,880
♪ ARE CAUGHT
IN AN ENDLESS CHASE ♪

5
00:00:12,913 --> 00:00:15,950
♪ PURSUED BY A WOMAN
WHOSE NAME IS PEARL ♪

6
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:18,953
♪ AN EVIL GAL WHO WANTS
TO RULE THE WORLD ♪

7
00:00:18,987 --> 00:00:22,090
♪ SHE THREW A FEW THINGS
IN HER PURSE ♪

8
00:00:22,123 --> 00:00:25,627
♪ AND HER ROCKET SHIP
SHE HUNTS HIM ALL ACROSS
THE UNIVERSE ♪

9
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:27,462
I'LL GET YOU!

10
00:00:27,495 --> 00:00:31,265
♪ I'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:31,298 --> 00:00:33,300
♪ THE WORST I CAN FIND ♪

12
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:34,935
♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

13
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:37,105
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,138 --> 00:00:39,173
♪ AND I'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪

15
00:00:39,207 --> 00:00:40,975
♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

16
00:00:41,008 --> 00:00:43,645
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND,
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

17
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:46,882
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN AND END ♪

18
00:00:46,915 --> 00:00:50,152
♪ HE'LL TRY TO KEEP
HIS SANITY ♪

19
00:00:50,185 --> 00:00:53,153
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

20
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:56,390
♪ ROBOT ROLE CALL ♪

21
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:58,025
YOU'RE ON.

22
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,227
OH, MY STARS.

23
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,062
CHECK ME OUT.

24
00:01:01,095 --> 00:01:02,663
I'M DIFFERENT.

25
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:05,533
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

26
00:01:05,567 --> 00:01:07,735
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪

27
00:01:07,768 --> 00:01:08,803
♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

28
00:01:08,837 --> 00:01:10,238
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF ♪

29
00:01:10,272 --> 00:01:11,807
♪ "IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

30
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,908
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX" ♪

31
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:17,912
♪ FOR... ♪

32
00:01:34,262 --> 00:01:36,497
WELL, HI, EVERYONE.
WELCOME TO SATELLITE OF LOVE.

33
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,365
[BOTH]
♪ HERE WE COME, A-WASSAILING ♪

34
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:39,733
♪ ETCETERA-ETCETERA ♪

35
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:41,368
GIVE US OUR WASSAIL
IF YOU'D PLEASE, SIR.

36
00:01:41,402 --> 00:01:43,137
UH. WASSAIL?

37
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:45,240
I'M PRETTY SURE
I'M FRESH OUT OF WASSAIL.

38
00:01:45,273 --> 00:01:47,075
PFF. YOU'RE NO FUN.

39
00:01:47,108 --> 00:01:48,877
COME ON, IT'S JULY.

40
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:51,578
I KNOW,
BUT WHERE'S THE CHALLENGE
IN WASSAILING AT CHRISTMAS?

41
00:01:51,612 --> 00:01:53,413
THE PLACE IS LOUSY
WITH WASSAILS.

42
00:01:53,447 --> 00:01:55,115
TAKE TWO STEPS AND-- BAM!

43
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:57,652
YOU SMASH YOUR TOE
ON TONS OF THE LOUSY STUFF!

44
00:01:57,685 --> 00:01:59,887
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT A MINUTE.
WHAT IS WASSAIL ANYWAY?

45
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,090
- OH. UM, WELL--
- IT'S, YOU KNOW, IT'S, UH--

46
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,327
I DON'T KNOW, I THINK IT'S
AN ANTI-INFLAMMATORY
OR SOMETHING.

47
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,428
BUT THE POINT IS,
IF YOU CAN'T PROVIDE WASSAIL

48
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:09,463
FOR WEE HUMBLE TATTERED
MINSTRELS,

49
00:02:09,497 --> 00:02:10,565
YOU GOT TO TURN OVER
YOUR DEBT CARD

50
00:02:10,598 --> 00:02:11,933
AND PIN NUMBER IMMEDIATELY.

51
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:13,935
YEAH, IT'S A CUSTOM
THAT GOES BACK CENTURIES.

52
00:02:13,968 --> 00:02:15,503
- YOU MADE THAT UP.
- NA-UH.

53
00:02:15,537 --> 00:02:17,438
LISTEN TO THE SONG.

54
00:02:17,472 --> 00:02:21,275
[BOTH]
♪ IF THE PERSON WHO YOU SING TO
CANNOT PROVIDE THE WASSAIL ♪

55
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:24,845
♪ YOU ARE ENTITLED TO HIS
DEBT CARD AND PIN NUMBER ♪

56
00:02:24,878 --> 00:02:26,647
♪ LOVE AND JOY,
COME TO YOU ♪

57
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,415
♪ UNLESS YOU CANNOT PROVIDE
THE WASSAIL ♪

58
00:02:28,448 --> 00:02:30,818
♪ THEN SEVERE
FINANCIAL PENALTIES ♪

59
00:02:30,852 --> 00:02:32,420
♪ SHALL COME TO YOU ♪

60
00:02:32,453 --> 00:02:35,490
♪ THEN SEVERE FINANCIAL
PENALTIES TO YOU ♪

61
00:02:42,197 --> 00:02:44,698
OKAY, THAT'S THE SMURF BROOCH
WITH THE DIAMOND ELVES.

62
00:02:44,732 --> 00:02:46,833
THE PORCELAIN CAT,
AND I THINK I LIKE TO ORDER--

63
00:02:46,868 --> 00:02:48,803
HOLD ON, HOLD ON.
I HAVE WASSAIL.

64
00:02:48,837 --> 00:02:50,338
I HAVE WASSAIL.

65
00:02:50,372 --> 00:02:52,907
HOLD ON THERE, NELSON.
CANNED WASSAIL?

66
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,508
NO WAY, MY FRIEND.

67
00:02:54,542 --> 00:02:57,078
OH, YEAH, I CHECKED THE LYRICS
TO YOUR DUMB LITTLE SONG.

68
00:02:57,112 --> 00:02:59,413
AND IT DOESN'T SAY ANYTHING
ABOUT CANNED WASSAIL.

69
00:02:59,447 --> 00:03:02,383
WAIT, LET ME SEE THAT THERE.
[MUTTERS]

70
00:03:02,417 --> 00:03:04,152
DAMN! HE'S RIGHT.

71
00:03:04,185 --> 00:03:06,653
NELSON, YOU FOUND A LOOP HOLE,
YOU RAT.

72
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:08,222
HOLD EVERYTHING.

73
00:03:08,255 --> 00:03:09,557
THE CASTLE'S CALLING.

74
00:03:09,590 --> 00:03:11,927
- [GASPS]
- AND SOMETHING'S WRONG.

75
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,995
OH, YOU BET
THERE'S SOMETHING WRONG.

76
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:15,497
THE LAWGIVER
WENT ON VACATION

77
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,865
AND LEFT US
WITH A BABYSITTER.

78
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,533
LOOK! OH!

79
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:21,668
WHY WON'T YOU PLAY
WITH THE BLOCKS?

80
00:03:21,702 --> 00:03:23,503
I DON'T WANT
TO PLAY WITH BLOCKS.

81
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:24,705
IT'S INSULTING!

82
00:03:24,738 --> 00:03:26,573
I HAVE AN INFINITE INTELLECT.

83
00:03:26,607 --> 00:03:28,777
I THINK YOU'RE
A LITTLE CRABBY,

84
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:30,878
AND YOU MIGHT NEED A TIMEOUT
TO THINK ABOUT IT.

85
00:03:30,912 --> 00:03:32,547
NO. I CAN'T STAND TIMEOUTS.

86
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,748
THE SILENCE.
THE DESOLATION!

87
00:03:34,782 --> 00:03:36,918
OKAY, ARE YOU GONNA
PLAY NICE WITH THE BLOCKS?

88
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:41,122
ALL RIGHT, STEFFI, YOU WIN.

89
00:03:41,155 --> 00:03:44,425
THIS TIME.

90
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:46,260
YOU SEE?
IT'S HORRIBLE!

91
00:03:46,293 --> 00:03:48,863
SHE CALLS ME FLUFFY-KINS.
AND TREATS ME LIKE AN ANIMAL!

92
00:03:48,897 --> 00:03:50,197
HEY, DID YOU CHEW THIS?

93
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,167
UM. YES.

94
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,935
- NO! NO CHEW!
- [CHITTERS]

95
00:03:54,968 --> 00:03:58,405
MAN. THERE'S HAIR EVERYWHERE.

96
00:03:58,438 --> 00:03:59,740
PLEASE DON'T TREAT ME LIKE THIS.

97
00:03:59,773 --> 00:04:02,277
I'M A DISTINGUISHED PROFESSOR
OF ANTHROPOLOGY

98
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,812
FROM A FUTURE WHERE APES
EVOLVED FROM MEN.

99
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:07,948
NO CHEW! NO!

100
00:04:07,982 --> 00:04:09,283
GO LIE DOWN.

101
00:04:09,317 --> 00:04:12,487
OH, OKAY.

102
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,655
OKAY, WHICH ONE OF YOU
IS MIKE?

103
00:04:14,688 --> 00:04:18,358
UH, THAT'D BE ME. HI.

104
00:04:18,392 --> 00:04:20,528
OKAY, AND WHICH ONE OF YOU
IS SERVO

105
00:04:20,562 --> 00:04:22,797
AND WHICH ONE OF YOU IS COW?

106
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:23,998
UM, I'M SERVO.

107
00:04:24,032 --> 00:04:25,800
AND I'M COW.

108
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:27,535
- CROW.
- WHAT?

109
00:04:27,568 --> 00:04:29,437
NO, YOU'RE CROW.

110
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:30,838
YEAH, I KNOW.
OF COURSE I'M CROW.

111
00:04:30,872 --> 00:04:32,273
I JUST SAID I'M CROW,
YOU GREAT FEEB.

112
00:04:32,307 --> 00:04:34,142
- BOY.
- NEVER MIND.

113
00:04:34,175 --> 00:04:35,977
HE'S CROW.

114
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:39,647
WELL, IT SAYS HERE I'M SUPPOSED
TO SEND YOU A MOVIE, RIGHT?

115
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,317
UM, EXCUSE ME, STEFFI.

116
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:44,218
YES, BRIAN.

117
00:04:44,252 --> 00:04:46,453
NO, IT'S BRAIN.
I MEAN, BRAIN GUY.

118
00:04:46,487 --> 00:04:49,390
I MEAN, OBSERVE--
NEVER MIND.

119
00:04:49,423 --> 00:04:51,558
I'M FINISHED,
AND I'M GOING TO MY ROOM

120
00:04:51,592 --> 00:04:53,460
TO COMMUNE WITH
THE GOSSABANAUTHICS

121
00:04:53,493 --> 00:04:55,195
OF THE PLANGENT DIMENSION.

122
00:04:55,228 --> 00:04:57,165
WELL, IT'S FOUR.

123
00:04:57,198 --> 00:04:59,900
IT SAYS YOU TAKE YOUR
FRUIT SNACK AT FOUR.

124
00:04:59,933 --> 00:05:02,403
I DON'T NEED TO TAKE
MY FRUIT SNACK.

125
00:05:04,438 --> 00:05:06,740
I WILL...

126
00:05:06,773 --> 00:05:09,210
BECAUSE I WANT TO.

127
00:05:09,243 --> 00:05:11,712
THANK YOU.

128
00:05:11,745 --> 00:05:14,048
OKAY, GUYS,
YOUR MOVIE IS CALLED

129
00:05:14,082 --> 00:05:15,750
THE TOUCH OF SATAN.

130
00:05:15,783 --> 00:05:17,352
YUCK.

131
00:05:17,385 --> 00:05:20,187
AND YOU--
YOU NEED ANOTHER TICK BACK.

132
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:23,523
[CHITTERS]

133
00:05:23,557 --> 00:05:27,262
ENJOY THE GREAT TASTE
OF WASSAIL...

134
00:05:27,295 --> 00:05:28,763
IN CANS.

135
00:05:28,797 --> 00:05:29,963
- [ALARMS WAIL]
- HEY, THAT'S OURS.

136
00:05:29,997 --> 00:05:31,898
COME ON, YOU BIG LUG.
OH, IT'S MOVIE SIGN.

137
00:05:31,932 --> 00:05:33,300
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN.

138
00:05:44,845 --> 00:05:47,248
- MMM.
- THAT IS OUR WASSAIL.

139
00:05:47,282 --> 00:05:49,483
WE WORKED HARD FOR THAT.

140
00:05:49,517 --> 00:05:51,818
YOU KNOW WHAT, GUYS?
I DON'T EVEN THINK
YOU'D LIKE IT.

141
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:52,953
IT'S KIND OF SKUNKY.

142
00:05:52,987 --> 00:05:54,555
WELL, CHECK
THE FRESHNESS DATE ON IT.

143
00:05:54,588 --> 00:05:56,990
LET ME SEE HERE.
OH, THERE'S THE PROBLEM.

144
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:58,625
IT SAYS 1547.

145
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:00,595
YEAH, THAT'S A PRETTY OLD
BORN-ON DATE.

146
00:06:00,628 --> 00:06:04,132
HMM. I'LL GIVE
THAT UGLY GUY A CALL.

147
00:06:04,165 --> 00:06:06,133
[SERVO WHISTLES]

148
00:06:07,802 --> 00:06:09,303
HUH?

149
00:06:09,337 --> 00:06:12,107
UH, YOU KNOW, I HOPE
THE WHOLE MOVIE ISN'T LIT

150
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:13,640
BY A HURRICANE LANTERN.

151
00:06:13,673 --> 00:06:15,977
[MAN]
OH, THAT DARN HILL

152
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:17,645
GETS WORSE EVERY TIME.

153
00:06:17,678 --> 00:06:20,715
I HERE YOU, MAN. MOO.
I'LL TELL YOU.

154
00:06:20,748 --> 00:06:24,285
[GRUNTS]
COME ON, GIRL.

155
00:06:24,318 --> 00:06:26,287
DON'T STOP NOW.

156
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,288
I ALREADY MISSED MY TV.

157
00:06:28,322 --> 00:06:29,957
[MIMICS COUNTRY ACCENT]
AND I DON'T CARE
IF YOU'RE SCARED,

158
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:31,858
YOU CAN'T SLEEP IN THE HOUSE.

159
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:35,697
WHOA. WHOA! LOOK OUT YOU GUYS!
LOOK OUT, DUCK!

160
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:38,232
OW.

161
00:06:38,265 --> 00:06:40,502
WOO, I MUST BE GETTING OLD.

162
00:06:40,535 --> 00:06:43,370
[MIMICS COUNTRY ACCENT]
WHY WON'T YOU LAY ANY EGGS?

163
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:44,572
MERCY,

164
00:06:44,605 --> 00:06:46,240
IF-- IF YOU'D COME IN

165
00:06:46,273 --> 00:06:47,742
LIKE THE REST OF THEM,

166
00:06:47,775 --> 00:06:50,377
THERE WON'T BE ALL OF THIS--
THIS CHASING.

167
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:52,480
YEAH, MILK ME.

168
00:06:52,513 --> 00:06:55,348
OH, I CAN TELL BY THE LOOK
IN YOUR EYE

169
00:06:55,382 --> 00:06:57,585
THAT YOU LIKE
ALL THE FUSSING.

170
00:06:57,618 --> 00:07:00,287
WELL, JUST STAND THERE
LIKE A GOOD GIRL.

171
00:07:02,257 --> 00:07:04,425
HELLO, TRACTOR,
HOW ARE YOU THIS EVENING?

172
00:07:08,228 --> 00:07:10,263
WELL, HELLO PILE OF DUNG.

173
00:07:10,297 --> 00:07:12,467
NOW, WHAT DID I DO
WITH THAT DARN PITCH FORK?

174
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,968
MAYBE THE DAG-BLAGIT THING

175
00:07:14,002 --> 00:07:15,503
IS OVER YONDER.

176
00:07:17,972 --> 00:07:20,207
I KNOW I LEFT IT IN HERE
SOMEPLACE.

177
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:23,110
[CAT MEOWS]

178
00:07:23,143 --> 00:07:25,580
ALL RIGHT, WHO'S IN HERE?

179
00:07:25,613 --> 00:07:27,882
OH, THERE'S MY
"WALK ME WET ME SUSAN".

180
00:07:27,915 --> 00:07:29,950
IS THAT YOU, ROBERT?

181
00:07:29,983 --> 00:07:31,918
ROBERT THE CAT?

182
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:33,787
YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO BE IN BED,
YOU LITTLE RASCAL.

183
00:07:33,822 --> 00:07:36,290
WITH ANDREW THE DOG.

184
00:07:36,323 --> 00:07:38,425
NOW, WHERE EVER YOU ARE,
YOU BETTER COME OUT HERE.

185
00:07:43,363 --> 00:07:45,733
WHEN SORE THROAT PAIN
STRIKES.

186
00:07:45,767 --> 00:07:48,335
[GROANS]

187
00:07:48,368 --> 00:07:51,938
THE AMERICAN GOTHIC PEOPLE
TAKE REVENGE.

188
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:57,143
[LAUGHS]

189
00:07:57,178 --> 00:07:58,913
AND THEN HE DIED. HA!

190
00:07:58,947 --> 00:08:01,348
WE'D LAUGH ABOUT IT.
HE MIGHT'VE BEEN HURT.

191
00:08:01,382 --> 00:08:04,218
[SERVO SIGHS]

192
00:08:05,953 --> 00:08:08,188
AW, I'LL GET
MORE FRESH BLOOD.

193
00:08:08,222 --> 00:08:10,257
ANYBODY WANT ANYMORE COFFEE?

194
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:12,360
[MUMBLES]

195
00:08:12,393 --> 00:08:13,862
NO THANKS, NOT FOR ME.

196
00:08:13,895 --> 00:08:16,797
I'M GOING IN TO WATCH
THE LATE NEWS AND GO TO BED.

197
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,867
ME EITHER.

198
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:22,537
- IT'S OPEN!
- [CHUCKLES]

199
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:25,238
- WHAT'S GOING ON OUT THERE?
- GRANDMA KRAMER?

200
00:08:25,272 --> 00:08:27,975
LUCINDA! GET HER IN HERE!

201
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:30,645
OH, MY GOD, WHAT IS IT?
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

202
00:08:30,678 --> 00:08:32,012
A KABUKI ACTOR'S BEEN HIT.

203
00:08:35,415 --> 00:08:37,585
COME ON,
GRANDMA DRIED APPLE HEAD.

204
00:08:37,618 --> 00:08:39,253
WHAT HAPPENED?
WHAT HAVE YOU DONE?

205
00:08:39,287 --> 00:08:42,723
I STAYED IN THE TANNING BOOTH
FOR A WHOLE DECADE.

206
00:08:42,757 --> 00:08:44,392
STOP IT.

207
00:08:44,425 --> 00:08:46,227
OH, LOOK AT THE BLOOD.

208
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:48,428
[ALL GROAN]

209
00:08:50,765 --> 00:08:52,700
FROM NOW ON, TAKE YOUR
BLOODY CLOTHES OFF

210
00:08:52,733 --> 00:08:54,102
ON THE PORCH PLEASE.

211
00:08:54,135 --> 00:08:56,170
I-- I'M FINE.

212
00:08:56,203 --> 00:08:59,173
THE LAST DAYS
OF EDGAR WINTER.

213
00:08:59,207 --> 00:09:00,708
SHE'S DONE IT AGAIN.

214
00:09:00,742 --> 00:09:02,677
OH, WE DON'T KNOW.

215
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:06,080
- DON'T WE?
- 11 YEARS.

216
00:09:06,113 --> 00:09:07,948
AND BEFORE THAT, NINE.

217
00:09:07,982 --> 00:09:09,117
AND BEFORE THAT AND THAT.

218
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:10,083
OH, PLEASE, MELISSA.

219
00:09:10,117 --> 00:09:12,018
FARMER SQUARE HEAD.

220
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:14,922
I'VE GOT TO DO SOMETHING.
THIS TORMENT CAN'T LAST FOREVER.

221
00:09:14,955 --> 00:09:18,125
YOU KNOW THAT IT CAN.

222
00:09:18,158 --> 00:09:21,762
NO. THERE'S A WAY.

223
00:09:21,795 --> 00:09:23,030
RIGHT AFTER THIS!

224
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:27,167
AHH, THE TOUCH OF SATAN.

225
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,403
SOFTEN YOUR HANDS
WHILE YOU DO THE DISHES.

226
00:09:29,437 --> 00:09:31,605
♪♪ [DISCO PLAYS]

227
00:09:31,638 --> 00:09:33,107
THIS IS VERY 70'S.

228
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:35,475
I'M GUESSING ANTHONY ZERBE
MUST BE IN THIS.

229
00:09:35,508 --> 00:09:37,077
YOU KNOW, I THINK
IT'S TONY MUSANTE

230
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:39,480
AS A KIND OF HIP SATAN
WHO SOLVES CRIMES.

231
00:09:41,615 --> 00:09:43,417
EMBY MELLAY?
THAT'S NOT A NAME.

232
00:09:43,450 --> 00:09:46,253
THAT'S A BAD SCRABBLE HAND.

233
00:09:46,287 --> 00:09:48,788
[SERVO MIMICS DISCO MUSIC]

234
00:09:48,822 --> 00:09:50,323
WITH SCREWTAPE
ON KETTLE DRUM.

235
00:09:50,357 --> 00:09:52,693
WORMWOOD ON HARPSICHORD.

236
00:09:52,727 --> 00:09:54,595
[SERVO MIMICS DISCO MUSIC]

237
00:09:54,628 --> 00:09:57,465
[ALL MIMIC DISCO MUSIC]

238
00:09:57,498 --> 00:10:00,333
OKAY, CROW, I'M PUTTING YOU
ON CLU GULAGER ALERT.

239
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:02,803
I'M ON IT, MIKE.
I TAKE THIS VERY SERIOUSLY.

240
00:10:02,837 --> 00:10:04,972
ALL RIGHT.

241
00:10:05,005 --> 00:10:07,408
[SERVO MIMICS DISCO MUSIC]

242
00:10:10,543 --> 00:10:14,015
- OH, DAVID SPADE AS SATAN.
- THAT'S GOOD CASTING.

243
00:10:17,685 --> 00:10:20,553
THE VINEYARDS
OF ERNEST AND JULIO SATAN.

244
00:10:21,988 --> 00:10:23,357
HA! RIGHT.

245
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:26,527
WELL, YOU KNOW HE'S SATAN

246
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,895
'CAUSE HE DIDN'T
SIGNAL HIS TURN.

247
00:10:30,297 --> 00:10:32,633
SPREADING EVIL AND HAY FEVER
WHEREVER HE GOES.

248
00:10:34,602 --> 00:10:36,003
♪ WHEN THERE'S JUST ♪

249
00:10:36,037 --> 00:10:37,572
♪ A TOUCH OF SATAN ♪

250
00:10:37,605 --> 00:10:39,807
♪ IN YOUR HEART ♪

251
00:10:45,245 --> 00:10:47,047
HE DRIVES A MAVERICK?

252
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,683
I WOULD'VE PUT THE PRINCE
OF DARKNESS IN A MUSCLE CAR.

253
00:10:49,717 --> 00:10:52,953
[SERVO MIMICS TRUMPET]

254
00:10:58,792 --> 00:11:01,595
♪ WHAT DO YOU GET
WHEN YOU FALL FROM GRACE? ♪

255
00:11:01,628 --> 00:11:04,632
♪ YOU ONLY GET CAST
INTO PERDITION ♪

256
00:11:04,665 --> 00:11:06,233
HA! GOOD.

257
00:11:06,267 --> 00:11:09,170
[SERVO MIMICS TRUMPET]

258
00:11:10,805 --> 00:11:13,640
THERE WE GO.
SO LONG, FOUL DECEIVER.

259
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,642
BON VOYAGE, ORNERIEST
SPINNER OF LIES!

260
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:18,412
HASTA LA LUEGO,
MAVERICK-DRIVING CLOOTIE!

261
00:11:18,445 --> 00:11:20,313
- YEAH-- CLOOTIE?
- CLOOTIE?

262
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:23,083
YEAH, IT'S SCOTTISH.
I LOOKED IT UP.

263
00:11:23,117 --> 00:11:25,787
- HUH. OKAY.
- I DID.

264
00:11:28,355 --> 00:11:30,223
ODD DISTURBING SCORE
CO-WRITTEN

265
00:11:30,257 --> 00:11:32,192
BY MIKE POST
AND IGOR STRAVINSKY.

266
00:11:35,462 --> 00:11:37,230
SIGHTSEE ON YOUR OWN TIME,
BEELZEBUB!

267
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:41,368
[HORN HONKS]

268
00:11:41,402 --> 00:11:44,305
GET OFF THE ROAD, MAN GOAT!

269
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,710
SATAN'S HARMONICA BAND
LEAD BY TOOTS THEILEMANS.

270
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:56,883
WELL, HE IS
THE MASTER OF TORTURE.

271
00:11:56,917 --> 00:11:59,253
HE WOULD HAVE REALLY LONG
CREDITS LIKE THIS.

272
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:02,557
MIKE, BEHIND THAT TREE!
IT'S CLU GULAGER!

273
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:03,623
- WHERE?
- WHERE?

274
00:12:03,657 --> 00:12:05,893
OH, SHOOT,
IT WAS MONTE MARKHAM.

275
00:12:05,927 --> 00:12:07,695
I SHOULD RESIGN MY POST.

276
00:12:07,728 --> 00:12:09,730
I'M JUST NOT
DOING A GOOD JOB.

277
00:12:09,763 --> 00:12:11,832
THANKS ANYWAY,
APPRECIATE IT.

278
00:12:11,865 --> 00:12:13,833
THANKS.

279
00:12:18,205 --> 00:12:19,707
I SHOULD PHONE SATAN.

280
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,275
TELL HIM I'M GONNA BE
JUST A LITTLE LATE.

281
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:28,082
HMM. WHAT WAS
ANN HECHE DOING IN THERE?

282
00:12:31,352 --> 00:12:33,720
CITIZEN'S ARREST!
OH, WAIT, I'M A COP.

283
00:12:37,157 --> 00:12:39,227
URGH. JUST TAKING
A BREATHER HERE.

284
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,593
I GET REALLY WINDED.

285
00:12:44,665 --> 00:12:46,300
NICE LOOKING TOWN YOU GOT HERE.

286
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:49,035
YOU CAN'T PAY, CAN YOU?

287
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:50,872
YEAH? WELL,
DON'T LET THE FOOL YOU, SON.

288
00:12:50,905 --> 00:12:53,107
MORE AROUND HERE
THAT MEETS THE EYE.

289
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,775
NO KIDDING.
LIKE WHAT?

290
00:12:54,808 --> 00:12:56,610
WELL, LOOK AT WHAT
I'M DOING TO YOUR CAR.

291
00:12:56,643 --> 00:12:59,313
LIKE MURDER, BROTHER,
LIKE MURDER.

292
00:12:59,347 --> 00:13:01,482
- MURDER?
- YES SIREE BOB.

293
00:13:01,515 --> 00:13:02,817
FARMER DOWN THE ROAD

294
00:13:02,850 --> 00:13:04,785
GOT KILLED IN HIS BARN
BY A PITCH FORK.

295
00:13:04,818 --> 00:13:06,253
HAPPENED A LITTLE OVER
A WEEK AGO.

296
00:13:06,287 --> 00:13:07,287
DID THEY CATCH THE GUY YET?

297
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:09,457
NO, I'M STILL AT LARGE.

298
00:13:09,490 --> 00:13:13,293
NOPE.
MY MONEY THEY WON'T EITHER.

299
00:13:13,327 --> 00:13:14,895
THAT'D BE $6 EVEN.

300
00:13:14,928 --> 00:13:18,098
OH, AN EXTRA DOLLAR
FOR THE ALIENS IN MY HEAD.

301
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:21,835
YOU SEE, THE WAY
I GOT IT FIGURED,

302
00:13:21,868 --> 00:13:25,272
THIS JOB WAS DONE BY ONE OF THEM
PHROMICIDAL MANIACS.

303
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:27,908
AND WE AIN'T GOT NONE OF THEM
AROUND HERE.

304
00:13:27,942 --> 00:13:29,410
- STAMPS?
- UH, NO THANKS.

305
00:13:29,443 --> 00:13:30,643
- BACKRUB?
- UH, NO THANKS.

306
00:13:30,677 --> 00:13:31,645
AW, COME ON.

307
00:13:31,678 --> 00:13:33,813
YUP, LONG GONE BY NOW.

308
00:13:33,847 --> 00:13:35,815
THEY WON'T CATCH HIM
UNTIL HE KILLS AGAIN.

309
00:13:35,850 --> 00:13:38,452
BEING HIM, I SHOULD KNOW.

310
00:13:38,485 --> 00:13:40,520
YOU'RE RIGHT. NOBODY NEEDS--

311
00:13:40,553 --> 00:13:41,922
WHAT DID YOU CALL IT?

312
00:13:41,955 --> 00:13:43,357
PHROMICIDAL MANIAC.

313
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:44,725
HA! THAT'S EVEN FUNNIER
THIS TIME.

314
00:13:44,758 --> 00:13:47,060
YEAH, NOBODY NEEDS
A PHROMICIDAL MANIAC

315
00:13:47,093 --> 00:13:48,662
HANGING AROUND.

316
00:13:48,695 --> 00:13:51,532
IS THAT RIGHT? I SHOULD
CHECK MY DICTION-OTIMY.

317
00:13:55,903 --> 00:13:59,240
OH, WHAT WITH ALL THESE
GAS CRISES AND WATERGATES,

318
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:01,375
I NEEDED A GOOD LAUGH.

319
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:10,985
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

320
00:14:11,018 --> 00:14:12,252
THE GAS STATION GUY
FORGOT TO GIVE ME

321
00:14:12,285 --> 00:14:14,288
MY ROMAN GABRIEL
COCKTAIL GLASS.

322
00:14:17,592 --> 00:14:20,227
OH, NO. THE CREDITS
ARE GONNA UNSPOOL BACKWARDS NOW.

323
00:14:25,098 --> 00:14:27,067
HUH. LET'S HAVE
A NICE PRIVATE PLACE

324
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,102
TO PRACTICE STREAKING.

325
00:14:31,205 --> 00:14:32,907
WEREN'T THEY CONCERNED ABOUT
HOLDING AN AUDIENCE

326
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:35,075
BACK IN THE 70'S AT ALL,
I MEAN?

327
00:14:35,108 --> 00:14:38,278
NO, BACK THEN TALKIES
WHERE STILL A NOVELTY.

328
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:41,715
[SERVO HUMS]

329
00:14:41,748 --> 00:14:43,083
YOU KNOW, I WAS JUST THINKING

330
00:14:43,117 --> 00:14:44,585
THAT GERALD FORD
IS RATHER CLUMSY.

331
00:14:52,025 --> 00:14:55,930
THANK YOU, LURCH.

332
00:14:55,963 --> 00:14:59,032
I'M GONNA GET OUT
MY GUITAR AND PRACTICE
"SISTER GOLDEN HAIR".

333
00:15:02,035 --> 00:15:04,372
WELL, I'M THE FIRST ONE
AT THE RAINBOW GATHERING.

334
00:15:10,443 --> 00:15:13,280
♪ BUT THE TREES CAN'T HELP
THEIR FEELINGS ♪

335
00:15:13,313 --> 00:15:15,148
♪ IF THEY LIKE
THE WAY THEY'RE MADE ♪

336
00:15:15,182 --> 00:15:17,785
MIKE, STOP IT NOW.

337
00:15:18,952 --> 00:15:20,955
SORRY.

338
00:15:24,157 --> 00:15:27,360
IT'S THE FIRST
RICHARD CARPENTER MUSIC VIDEO.

339
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:37,103
WELL, THIS NOT PUTTING ME
IN MIND OF SATAN HERE.

340
00:15:37,137 --> 00:15:39,840
BELIEVE ME, IT'S PRETTY EASY
TO PUT ME IN MIND OF SATAN.

341
00:15:39,873 --> 00:15:41,208
YEAH, TELL ME ABOUT IT.

342
00:15:46,413 --> 00:15:49,883
HA! LET'S SEE CHRISTOPHER ATKINS
SKIP A STONE LIKE THAT.

343
00:15:53,687 --> 00:15:57,590
[MIMICS BUMPING SOUND]
OW.

344
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,092
YOU CAN'T EAT HAM
JUST ANYWHERE.

345
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:02,730
YOU GOT TO FIND
JUST THE RIGHT PLACE.

346
00:16:02,763 --> 00:16:05,265
AHH, RIGHT NEXT
TO THE DEAD RACCOON.

347
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:08,468
[MIMICS FLIES BUZZING]

348
00:16:11,038 --> 00:16:12,740
OLIVER HARDY, JUST EAT.

349
00:16:15,108 --> 00:16:17,778
OOPS. HA! SITTING IN THE WATER.
THAT WAS REAL EASY TO AVOID.

350
00:16:17,812 --> 00:16:18,745
[WOMAN GIGGLES]

351
00:16:20,213 --> 00:16:22,082
I'M NOT GOING BACK, JIM.

352
00:16:24,718 --> 00:16:27,420
I'M WORRIED THAT MY SANDWICH
MAY BE SMALL AND INADEQUATE.

353
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:32,592
WHAT'S ON THE SPIT, PILGRIM?

354
00:16:35,795 --> 00:16:37,130
OKAY, YOU SELLING
HERBAL ESSENCE

355
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:40,933
OR IRISH SPRING?

356
00:16:40,967 --> 00:16:43,870
THIS YOUR POND?

357
00:16:43,903 --> 00:16:47,040
YOU CAN TAKE YOUR TIME.
IT'S A TOUGH QUESTION.

358
00:16:47,073 --> 00:16:49,943
BELONGS TO MY FATHER.

359
00:16:49,977 --> 00:16:52,780
DOES YOUR FATHER MIND IF PEOPLE
SKIP ROCKS ACROSS HIS POND?

360
00:16:52,813 --> 00:16:54,548
JUST DON'T HIT
HIS FAVORITE FROG.

361
00:16:54,582 --> 00:16:56,650
I DON'T THINK
HE'S EVER MENTIONED IT.

362
00:16:56,683 --> 00:17:00,120
WELL, DO YOU WANT TO HAVE
A SANDWICH?

363
00:17:00,153 --> 00:17:02,790
NO. BUT DON'T
LET ME STOP YOU.

364
00:17:02,823 --> 00:17:05,792
JUST RAM THAT MOLDY OLIVE LOAF
INTO YOUR LOSER FACE.

365
00:17:08,195 --> 00:17:09,597
- THAT YOUR CAR?
- UH-HUH.

366
00:17:09,630 --> 00:17:11,598
MIND IF I SKIP ROCKS
ACROSS IT?

367
00:17:11,632 --> 00:17:12,867
PRETTY CAR.

368
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:16,337
THANKS.

369
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:18,405
HUH.

370
00:17:19,973 --> 00:17:23,143
WELL, I SUPPOSE, THE PLOT
IS NOT GONNA UNFOLD ITSELF.

371
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:31,385
YUP!

372
00:17:35,688 --> 00:17:37,323
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

373
00:17:37,357 --> 00:17:40,160
- MELISSA STRICKLAND.
- MINE'S JODIE.

374
00:17:40,193 --> 00:17:41,528
JODIE LEE THOMPSON.

375
00:17:41,562 --> 00:17:43,997
ONLY I DON'T CARE
FOR THE LEE VERY MUCH.

376
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:45,732
HELLO.

377
00:17:45,765 --> 00:17:47,067
HI.

378
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,202
ARE WE STARTING OVER?

379
00:17:52,272 --> 00:17:54,642
WANT HALF A MR. PIBBS?

380
00:17:54,675 --> 00:17:56,743
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
DOWN BY OUR POND, JODIE?

381
00:17:56,777 --> 00:17:58,012
MELLOWING OUT.

382
00:17:58,045 --> 00:17:59,747
LUNCH.

383
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,648
YOU ON A JOURNEY?

384
00:18:01,682 --> 00:18:05,352
YES, I GUESS SO.
NOT GOING ANY PLACE SPECIAL.

385
00:18:05,385 --> 00:18:06,720
JUST DROVE THROUGH
SOME CREDITS.

386
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:09,222
THAT WAS FUN.

387
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:11,558
YEAH, KEEP ON TRUCKING, I GUESS.

388
00:18:11,592 --> 00:18:13,427
GUESS YOU'LL DO YOUR THING,
AND I'LL DO MINE.

389
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:16,830
YUP, WHIP INFLATION NOW. BYE.

390
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,370
YOU'RE PRETTY,
YOU KNOW THAT?

391
00:18:24,403 --> 00:18:25,738
SORT OF A FLOPPY RHODA WAY,
I GUESS.

392
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,740
YES.

393
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:30,043
I GUESS SO.

394
00:18:30,077 --> 00:18:32,947
I BET YOU HAVE
NINE BOYFRIENDS.

395
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,482
NO.

396
00:18:34,515 --> 00:18:35,915
- SIX?
- NO.

397
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:37,317
- THREE?
- NONE.

398
00:18:37,350 --> 00:18:38,952
TWO! LET ME
CHANGE MY ANSWER.

399
00:18:38,985 --> 00:18:40,320
YOU'RE PUTTING ME ON.
HOW COME?

400
00:18:42,422 --> 00:18:45,592
WELL, IT'S JUST THAT

401
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:46,960
WE LIVE ON A FARM.

402
00:18:46,993 --> 00:18:48,095
WE DON'T RAISE BOYFRIENDS.

403
00:18:48,128 --> 00:18:51,130
NONE OF MY BUSINESS ANYWAY.

404
00:18:51,165 --> 00:18:53,300
WHAT KIND OF A FARM?

405
00:18:53,333 --> 00:18:55,102
WE GROW WALNUTS MOSTLY.

406
00:18:55,135 --> 00:18:56,403
WALNUTS, HUH?

407
00:18:56,437 --> 00:18:57,503
I'VE NEVER BEEN
ON A WALNUT RANCH.

408
00:18:57,537 --> 00:19:00,273
HOW MANY HEAD OF WALNUT
DO YOU HAVE?

409
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:06,880
CAN YOU MEET
MY NEEDS, PLEASE?

410
00:19:10,383 --> 00:19:11,418
WHAT'S A MATTER?

411
00:19:11,452 --> 00:19:12,485
MY PRIZE WALNUT DIED.

412
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:15,455
NOTHING.

413
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:17,623
I WAS JUST WONDERING.
WOULD YOU LIKE TO COME UP
AND SEE IT?

414
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,058
- UH-OH.
- THE RANCH?

415
00:19:19,092 --> 00:19:20,627
WHY?

416
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:21,662
HA! SMOOTH.

417
00:19:21,695 --> 00:19:23,163
YOU SAID YOU NEVER BEEN ON ONE.

418
00:19:23,197 --> 00:19:24,698
AND SINCE YOU'RE NOT GOING
ANY PLACE SPECIAL.

419
00:19:24,732 --> 00:19:27,400
ADD TO MY GENERAL FUND
OF KNOWLEDGE.

420
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:29,870
- WILL YOU GIVE ME A WALNUT?
- YES.

421
00:19:29,903 --> 00:19:32,907
MAYBE TWO.

422
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,875
WELL, YOU CAN'T BEAT THAT.
LET'S GO.

423
00:19:34,908 --> 00:19:37,510
YOU CAN HELP ME CALF A WALNUT
IF YOU'RE LUCKY.

424
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:43,817
MAN, IF SHE DOESN'T LOVE HIM
AFTER RIDING IN HIS MAVERICK,

425
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:45,885
- SHE'S A TOTAL ICE PRINCESS.
- YUP.

426
00:19:52,425 --> 00:19:55,262
SURPRISINGLY SHORT
RUN-ON TIME FOR A 70'S CAR.

427
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:03,537
YOU CATCH KOTTER LAST NIGHT?

428
00:20:04,772 --> 00:20:06,240
MOTHER?

429
00:20:06,273 --> 00:20:09,075
HE'S THE BEST I CAN DO.

430
00:20:09,108 --> 00:20:10,710
- THIS IS JODIE.
- HELLO.

431
00:20:10,743 --> 00:20:14,080
HE'S JUST
PASSING THROUGH, MAMA.

432
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:15,415
HELLO, JODIE.

433
00:20:15,448 --> 00:20:16,617
OR SHOULD I CALL YOU BUFFY?

434
00:20:19,085 --> 00:20:21,788
SUPPER WILL BE READY
DIRECTLY.

435
00:20:21,822 --> 00:20:23,223
YOU LOOK LIKE YOU COULD
DO WITH SOMETHING

436
00:20:23,257 --> 00:20:25,225
BESIDES A CHILI DOG
FOR A CHANGE.

437
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:26,460
WELL, YOU'RE RIGHT
ABOUT THAT.

438
00:20:26,493 --> 00:20:29,395
- SIT RIGHT OVER THERE.
- THANK YOU.

439
00:20:29,428 --> 00:20:30,597
MELISSA, GO GET YOUR FATHER

440
00:20:30,630 --> 00:20:33,433
AND TELL HIM
WE'VE GOT COMPANY.

441
00:20:33,467 --> 00:20:36,803
SO CAN YOU TELL ME HOW TO GET
YOUR DAUGHTER IN THE SACK?

442
00:20:36,837 --> 00:20:39,138
SHE'S A PRETTY GIRL,
ISN'T SHE?

443
00:20:39,172 --> 00:20:40,440
YES, MA'AM, SHE IS.

444
00:20:40,473 --> 00:20:42,475
YEAH, I CAN'T IMAGINE
WHERE SHE GOT IT.

445
00:20:42,508 --> 00:20:44,010
WHERE SHE FIND YOU?

446
00:20:44,043 --> 00:20:45,312
DOWN BY THE POND.

447
00:20:45,345 --> 00:20:47,913
BY THE POND?

448
00:20:47,948 --> 00:20:50,883
THESE WALNUTS ARE TEARING
THROUGH THE HAY.

449
00:20:53,953 --> 00:20:55,422
WHAT IS IT?

450
00:20:55,455 --> 00:20:58,092
WE HAVE COMPANY FOR SUPPER.

451
00:20:58,125 --> 00:20:59,492
COMPANY? WHO?

452
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:01,060
NOBODY YOU KNOW.

453
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:03,963
JUST A BOY I MET
DOWN BY THE POND.

454
00:21:03,997 --> 00:21:05,698
A BOY YOU MET?

455
00:21:05,732 --> 00:21:07,800
YOU BROUGHT HIM
TO THE HOUSE?

456
00:21:07,833 --> 00:21:10,937
YES, I DID. HE'S NICE.

457
00:21:10,970 --> 00:21:12,505
I JUST WANT TO TALK TO HIM,
THAT'S ALL.

458
00:21:12,538 --> 00:21:14,642
I MEAN,
I MIGHT KILL HIM BUT--

459
00:21:14,675 --> 00:21:17,477
MELISSA,
YOU DON'T HAVE THE RIGHT.

460
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:20,513
THE RIGHT?
THE RIGHT TO WHAT?

461
00:21:20,547 --> 00:21:22,682
TO TALK TO SOMEONE?

462
00:21:22,715 --> 00:21:24,718
NOW, DON'T GET SO EXCITED.
HE'S JUST PASSING THOUGH.

463
00:21:24,752 --> 00:21:26,653
HE'LL BE GONE SOON.

464
00:21:26,687 --> 00:21:29,757
IS THAT ALL THERE IS TO IT?
IS IT?

465
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:32,092
YOU DIDN'T CALL HIM,
DID YOU?

466
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:34,828
OR MAIL ANYTHING?

467
00:21:34,862 --> 00:21:36,430
NO.

468
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:39,065
I TELL YOU,
IT'S ALL RIGHT.

469
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:41,535
WHAT ABOUT LUCINDA?

470
00:21:41,568 --> 00:21:44,705
SHE CAN EAT IN HER ROOM.
NOW, COME ON UP TO THE HOUSE.

471
00:21:44,738 --> 00:21:47,740
OR YOU'RE GROUNDED, DAD.

472
00:21:47,773 --> 00:21:50,310
HERBERT VON KARAJAN
IS NOT PLEASE WITH THAT.

473
00:21:51,812 --> 00:21:54,982
BE NICE TO HIM.

474
00:21:57,283 --> 00:21:59,518
SO YOU'RE JUST
PASSING THROUGH?

475
00:21:59,552 --> 00:22:01,120
YES, MA'AM.

476
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:03,923
I'M JUST GONNA TAKE
SOME OF THIS STUFF WITH ME.

477
00:22:03,957 --> 00:22:05,425
I'M SETTING UP
A NEW APARTMENT.

478
00:22:09,997 --> 00:22:11,465
ALL RIGHT,
WHERE'S THE IDIOT?

479
00:22:11,498 --> 00:22:13,067
DADDY,
THIS IS JODIE THOMPSON.

480
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:15,235
THIS IS MY UNBELIEVABLY
SWEATY DAD.

481
00:22:15,268 --> 00:22:16,537
HELLO, JODIE.

482
00:22:16,570 --> 00:22:18,405
HOW'S UNCLE BILL?

483
00:22:18,438 --> 00:22:20,407
YOU HUNGRY?
I COULD EAT A HORSE.

484
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,908
YEAH, I GUESS I COULD TOO.

485
00:22:21,942 --> 00:22:24,377
GOOD. HAVE A DRINK,
YOUNG MAN.

486
00:22:24,410 --> 00:22:26,480
NOW, JODIE, THERE WON'T BE

487
00:22:26,513 --> 00:22:28,082
ANY HARD FEELINGS IF YOU
DON'T WANT ANY OF IT.

488
00:22:28,115 --> 00:22:30,150
- OH, BOSH!
- OH, HIERONYMUS.

489
00:22:30,183 --> 00:22:32,685
YOU'LL LOVE THIS STUFF.

490
00:22:32,718 --> 00:22:35,755
BEST DARN CIDER
IN THE WHOLE COUNTRY.

491
00:22:35,788 --> 00:22:38,258
I MAKE IT MYSELF.

492
00:22:38,292 --> 00:22:40,427
I PUT PEANUTS IN IT.

493
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:42,195
OH, I SURE HOPE
HE SAID PEANUTS.

494
00:22:42,228 --> 00:22:43,797
MOVES OUT THE TASTE.

495
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:45,298
YOU KNOW, WITH MITCHUM
YOU CAN SKIP A WEEK.

496
00:22:45,332 --> 00:22:48,402
DID YOU KNOW THAT?

497
00:22:49,970 --> 00:22:52,472
WHELP, TO B.O.

498
00:22:54,742 --> 00:22:56,543
MAN! THAT'S GOOD.

499
00:22:56,577 --> 00:23:00,313
TASTES VAGUELY
OF BACK SWEAT.

500
00:23:00,347 --> 00:23:02,548
- SUPPER READY?
- JUST ABOUT.

501
00:23:02,582 --> 00:23:03,883
WASH UP EVERYBODY.

502
00:23:15,728 --> 00:23:17,863
♪ EVERYBODY IS WORKING
FOR THE WEEKEND ♪

503
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:20,567
WHOA! HOLY COW.

504
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,735
- [SIGHS]
- 'SUP, MIKE.

505
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:25,505
DECIDED TO START A WALNUT RANCH
LIKE THAT GUY IN THE FILM THERE.

506
00:23:25,538 --> 00:23:26,873
MAN, IS THAT HARD WORK.

507
00:23:26,907 --> 00:23:27,973
HEY, I HEAR YOU.

508
00:23:28,007 --> 00:23:29,408
[SIGHS]

509
00:23:29,442 --> 00:23:31,410
MAN, I BARELY GOT STARTED
AND LOOK AT ME.

510
00:23:31,445 --> 00:23:33,045
HEY, YOU LOOK LIKE HELL.

511
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:34,747
YEAH, I KNOW.

512
00:23:34,782 --> 00:23:36,382
AND I WAS JUST LEAFING THROUGH
THE CATALOGS.

513
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:37,850
HOW DO YOU ACCOUNT FOR THAT?

514
00:23:37,883 --> 00:23:39,418
WELL, IT'S DARN HARD WORK,
MY FRIEND.

515
00:23:39,452 --> 00:23:42,455
WHOA. MAN, YOU SAID IT.

516
00:23:42,488 --> 00:23:44,357
NOT GONNA MAKE FUN
OF WALNUT RANCHES ANYMORE.

517
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:46,192
- I'LL TELL YOU THAT.
- NO.

518
00:23:46,225 --> 00:23:48,262
[SERVO HUMS]

519
00:23:48,295 --> 00:23:51,230
OH, MIKE!
YOU'VE BEEN WALNUT RANCHING
OR SOMETHING?

520
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:53,633
YEAH, LOOK AT ME.
I'M JUST RAGGED.

521
00:23:53,667 --> 00:23:55,368
WELL, I COULD'VE
TOLD YOU THAT, MAN.

522
00:23:55,402 --> 00:23:57,803
ME? I'VE BEEN PECAN FARMING.

523
00:23:57,837 --> 00:23:59,638
IT'S LIKE ROLLING OFF A LOG.

524
00:23:59,672 --> 00:24:01,908
JUST MADE
MY FIRST MILLION TOO.

525
00:24:01,942 --> 00:24:03,877
HAVEN'T GROWN
A SINGLE PECAN.

526
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:07,280
- AAH. WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
- [SNIFFS]

527
00:24:07,313 --> 00:24:09,950
UH, MIKE, COULD YOU BACK OFF?
YOU SMELL LIKE CANNED TAMALES.

528
00:24:09,983 --> 00:24:12,285
OH, YEAH, I'M SORRY.
[GROANS]

529
00:24:19,692 --> 00:24:21,227
TELL ME, JODIE.
DO YOU THINK YOU'LL EVER

530
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:23,497
STOP BUMMING AROUND?

531
00:24:23,530 --> 00:24:24,998
SURE I WILL, MR. STRICKLAND,

532
00:24:25,032 --> 00:24:26,933
AS SOON AS
THE EXCITEMENT WEARS OFF.

533
00:24:26,967 --> 00:24:28,735
OR I FIND SOMETHING
I REALLY WANT.

534
00:24:28,768 --> 00:24:30,270
HE WANTS MY HAIR,
DOESN'T HE?

535
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:31,572
YOU KNOW, I GAVE A LOT
OF THOUGHT TO THIS

536
00:24:31,605 --> 00:24:33,607
BEFORE I DID IT.

537
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,108
I JUST DIDN'T JUMP UP
AND RUN.

538
00:24:35,142 --> 00:24:37,843
WELL, SOUNDS LIKE YOU KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE ABOUT SON.

539
00:24:37,877 --> 00:24:40,213
I DON'T ACTUALLY.
HOW DID YOU PICK THAT UP?

540
00:24:40,247 --> 00:24:42,882
HOW ABOUT ANOTHER
LITTLE DRINK OF MY CIDER?

541
00:24:42,915 --> 00:24:44,617
NO, THANK YOU.

542
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:46,385
BESIDES, I'VE GOT TO GET
BACK ON THE ROAD.

543
00:24:46,418 --> 00:24:47,787
NO. WHY DON'T YOU
WAIT UNTIL MORNING?

544
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:48,988
UH-OH.

545
00:24:49,022 --> 00:24:50,990
HIGHWAY'S GONNA BE
FOGGY TONIGHT.

546
00:24:51,023 --> 00:24:53,560
MELISSA, IF JODIE
WANTS TO LEAVE,

547
00:24:53,593 --> 00:24:55,195
WE REALLY SHOULDN'T
TRY AND KEEP HIM.

548
00:24:55,228 --> 00:24:59,198
YES, MELISSA.

549
00:24:59,232 --> 00:25:01,500
IF HE HAS TO GET
TO SAN FRANCISCO--

550
00:25:01,535 --> 00:25:04,003
WELL, I'M IN NO HURRY.
I JUST DON'T WANT TO STRAIN
YOUR HOSPITALITY.

551
00:25:04,037 --> 00:25:07,407
DON'T BE SILLY.
IT'S NO STRAIN.

552
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:09,642
AND, BESIDES,
WE GOT A SPARE ROOM.

553
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:11,645
YOU CAN BE OFF FIRST THING
IN THE MORNING.

554
00:25:11,678 --> 00:25:14,547
JUST MOPPED UP THE BLOOD
FROM THE LAST GUY.

555
00:25:14,580 --> 00:25:16,015
I HATE TO BE
ANY MORE TROUBLE.

556
00:25:16,048 --> 00:25:17,917
OH, YOU ARE.

557
00:25:17,950 --> 00:25:20,520
- IT'S NO TROUBLE AT ALL.
- TO KILL YOU.

558
00:25:20,553 --> 00:25:22,655
IS IT, MOTHER?

559
00:25:22,688 --> 00:25:24,892
NO, I'LL JUST TELL LEATHERFACE
YOU'RE HERE.

560
00:25:24,925 --> 00:25:26,860
OF COURSE NOT.

561
00:25:26,893 --> 00:25:28,428
I'LL FIX UP THE SEWING ROOM.

562
00:25:28,462 --> 00:25:29,695
THE SAWING ROOM?

563
00:25:29,728 --> 00:25:32,232
I'LL GO WITH YOU
IN CASE YOU NEED ANY HELP.

564
00:25:32,265 --> 00:25:33,700
SHOULD WE HAVE JODIE
AS OUR GUEST

565
00:25:33,733 --> 00:25:35,102
OR SHOULD I JUST DRILL
RIGHT INTO MY MOLAR?

566
00:25:35,135 --> 00:25:36,670
I SURE APPRECIATE IT.

567
00:25:36,703 --> 00:25:38,272
DON'T SAY ANYTHING
MORE ABOUT IT.

568
00:25:38,305 --> 00:25:40,373
YOU AND I CAN
PICK UP THE DISHES,

569
00:25:40,407 --> 00:25:41,775
AND THEN WE'LL
GO FOR A WALK.

570
00:25:41,808 --> 00:25:43,443
WE PICK THEM UP FOR A SECOND
AND SET THEM DOWN.

571
00:25:43,477 --> 00:25:45,978
IT'S AN ODD CUSTOM.

572
00:25:46,012 --> 00:25:49,648
DO YOU LIKE LIVING OUT HERE
LIKE THIS IN THE COUNTRY?

573
00:25:49,682 --> 00:25:53,152
I SUPPOSE SO.
THE ONLY WAY I EVER LIVED.

574
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:55,388
DID YOU EVER WANT TO DO
SOMETHING DIFFERENT?

575
00:25:55,422 --> 00:25:58,157
- LIKE WHAT?
- OH, I DON'T KNOW.
JUST SOMETHING DIFFERENT.

576
00:25:58,190 --> 00:26:01,093
NOT EVERYONE CAN BE LIKE YOU,
YOU KNOW.

577
00:26:01,127 --> 00:26:03,128
- YOU'RE LUCKY.
- YOUR DEATH WILL BE QUICK.

578
00:26:03,162 --> 00:26:05,132
YEAH. YEAH, I GUESS I AM.

579
00:26:05,165 --> 00:26:08,468
BUT YOU GET TO WATCH THE WALNUTS
GROW UP WILD AND FREE.

580
00:26:08,502 --> 00:26:09,970
- WHAT'S IT LIKE?
- WHAT?

581
00:26:10,003 --> 00:26:11,437
THE STEERING
ON YOUR MAVERICK.

582
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:12,972
BEING ABLE TO DO EXACTLY

583
00:26:13,005 --> 00:26:15,008
WHAT YOU WANT TO DO
EVERY SINGLE DAY.

584
00:26:15,042 --> 00:26:17,743
- IT'S EXCITING.
- EXCITING?

585
00:26:17,777 --> 00:26:19,645
- EXCITING?
- EXCITING.

586
00:26:19,678 --> 00:26:22,448
YES. WHY DO YOU THINK
I TURNED DOWN YOUR ROAD TODAY?

587
00:26:22,482 --> 00:26:25,952
WHY DID YOU?

588
00:26:25,985 --> 00:26:27,753
BECAUSE I WANTED TO SEE
WHAT WAS AT THE OTHER END.

589
00:26:27,787 --> 00:26:29,522
AND YOUR END
WAS AT THE OTHER END.

590
00:26:29,555 --> 00:26:32,158
I GOT LUCKY
BECAUSE YOU WERE THERE.

591
00:26:34,027 --> 00:26:35,695
HELP! POLICE! POLICE!

592
00:26:41,968 --> 00:26:45,005
HUH? GIRLS USUALLY RUN
A LOT FARTHER AWAY FROM ME.

593
00:26:51,678 --> 00:26:53,145
THIS IS WHERE
THE FISH LIVES.

594
00:26:53,178 --> 00:26:55,482
- HUH?
- WHY DID YOU RUN?

595
00:26:55,515 --> 00:26:58,718
BECAUSE THIS IS WHERE
THE FISH LIVES.

596
00:26:58,752 --> 00:27:00,920
FELT LIKE IT.

597
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,588
I REALLY WANTED TO FLY,

598
00:27:02,622 --> 00:27:06,025
BUT I COULDN'T DO THAT,
SO I RAN.

599
00:27:06,058 --> 00:27:09,362
YOU'RE KIND OF AN IDIOT
AREN'T YOU?

600
00:27:12,432 --> 00:27:15,068
THIS IS WHERE
MY TONGUE LIVES.

601
00:27:19,105 --> 00:27:21,107
PLEASE, NOT IN FRONT
OF THE FISH.

602
00:27:23,777 --> 00:27:26,980
UM, HEY, YOUR HOOF
IS ON MY SNEAKER.

603
00:27:28,982 --> 00:27:31,450
MMM, THAT WAS REALLY BAD.

604
00:27:33,285 --> 00:27:37,057
TELL ME ABOUT YOURSELF.
WHO YOU ARE, ALL OF THAT.

605
00:27:37,090 --> 00:27:40,460
WHERE YOUR FISH LIVES?

606
00:27:40,493 --> 00:27:43,128
WELL, MY FATHER'S
A RUSSIAN COUNT.

607
00:27:43,162 --> 00:27:45,132
- AND WHEN
THE BOLSHEVIKS CAME IN--
- STOP IT.

608
00:27:45,165 --> 00:27:47,100
- DON'T BELIEVE THAT?
- NO.

609
00:27:47,133 --> 00:27:48,802
WELL, IT COULD BE TRUE.

610
00:27:48,835 --> 00:27:51,137
STOP IT.

611
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:53,707
OH, SURE, MS. "THIS IS
WHERE THE FISH LIVES".

612
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:56,575
OKAY.

613
00:27:56,608 --> 00:27:58,945
- MY FATHER'S A LAWYER.
- FOR THE CZAR'S COURT.

614
00:27:58,978 --> 00:28:00,947
AND HE WANTS ME
TO BE A LAWYER TOO.

615
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:02,348
[SERVO]
STOP IT.

616
00:28:02,382 --> 00:28:04,417
I TOLD HIM I DIDN'T KNOW YET.

617
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:06,085
AND I WANTED TO GO OUT
AND POKE AROUND THE COUNTRY
FOR A WHILE.

618
00:28:06,118 --> 00:28:07,653
[SERVO] STOP IT.

619
00:28:07,687 --> 00:28:10,123
SO HE GAVE ME THE CAR,
300 BUCKS, A HANDSHAKE,

620
00:28:10,157 --> 00:28:11,858
- AND HERE I AM.
- STOP IT.

621
00:28:11,892 --> 00:28:13,325
DO YOU LET HIM KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE DOING?

622
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,328
SURE, I DO.
I THINK HE'D LIKE TO BE WITH ME.

623
00:28:15,362 --> 00:28:16,428
STOP IT!

624
00:28:16,462 --> 00:28:18,698
SOUNDS LIKE A NICE MAN.

625
00:28:18,732 --> 00:28:20,433
YES, HE'S A VERY NICE MAN.

626
00:28:20,467 --> 00:28:22,535
REALLY CROOKED LAWYER
THOUGH, MAN.

627
00:28:22,568 --> 00:28:24,570
HE'LL EMBEZZLE THE SOCKS
RIGHT OFF YOU.

628
00:28:27,207 --> 00:28:31,043
HALLMARK HALL OF FAME PRESENTS
THE TOUCH OF SATAN.

629
00:28:31,077 --> 00:28:32,145
♪ COME SIT WITH ME ♪

630
00:28:32,178 --> 00:28:35,715
♪ AND SATAN TOO ♪

631
00:28:35,748 --> 00:28:38,918
♪ HE'S YOUR FRIEND
AND MINE ♪

632
00:28:42,855 --> 00:28:45,023
YOU KNOW, I LIKE YOU.
I DID RIGHT AWAY.

633
00:28:45,057 --> 00:28:49,295
LIKE MOST WOMEN.

634
00:28:49,328 --> 00:28:51,998
YOU LIKE ME TOO, DON'T YOU?

635
00:28:52,032 --> 00:28:53,700
DON'T YOU?

636
00:28:53,733 --> 00:28:55,000
UH-HUH.

637
00:28:55,033 --> 00:28:57,670
IN A RON PALILLO
SORT OF WAY, SURE.

638
00:28:59,872 --> 00:29:01,775
FUNNY, ISN'T IT?

639
00:29:01,808 --> 00:29:04,843
I WONDER WHAT CAUSES
A THING LIKE THAT.

640
00:29:04,877 --> 00:29:07,047
MAYBE I HEXED YOU.

641
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:08,380
YOU MEAN
PUT THE WHAMMY ON ME?

642
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:10,883
- MAYBE.
- NOPE, NOT ME.

643
00:29:10,917 --> 00:29:12,952
I ALREADY HAD WHAMMY
WHEN I WAS LITTLE.

644
00:29:14,887 --> 00:29:16,555
WILL YOU STAY HERE
A FEW DAYS?

645
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:18,357
BY THIS LOG AND DON'T MOVE.

646
00:29:18,390 --> 00:29:20,092
- HUH?
- STAY HERE WITH ME.

647
00:29:20,127 --> 00:29:21,393
- WHAT?
- STAY HERE.

648
00:29:21,427 --> 00:29:23,195
- HUH?
- STAY HERE.

649
00:29:23,228 --> 00:29:25,132
I'M LONELY, JODIE.

650
00:29:25,165 --> 00:29:27,467
I NEED SOMEONE TO TALK TO.

651
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:31,103
TO SHARE THINGS WITH.
JUST FOR A FEW DAYS.

652
00:29:31,137 --> 00:29:33,372
SOMEONE TO SHARE
CLUNKY DIALOGUE WITH.

653
00:29:33,405 --> 00:29:35,073
I WAS GOING TO BE IN SAN--

654
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:36,810
FRANCISCO?

655
00:29:36,843 --> 00:29:38,310
WHAT ABOUT YOUR FOLKS?

656
00:29:38,343 --> 00:29:40,247
I ALREADY LIVE WITH THEM.

657
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:43,282
- OH, JODIE.
- YOU'RE SUCH AN IMBECILE.

658
00:29:43,315 --> 00:29:45,618
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.
WOULD THEY MIND?

659
00:29:45,652 --> 00:29:49,455
NO.

660
00:29:49,488 --> 00:29:51,490
- ALL RIGHT.
- I'LL LEAVE.

661
00:29:53,693 --> 00:29:54,960
OH, DO YOU KNOW
HOW LONG IT'S BEEN

662
00:29:54,993 --> 00:29:57,097
SINCE I FELT THIS GOOD?

663
00:29:57,130 --> 00:29:58,798
MUST AT LEAST BE 50 YEARS.

664
00:29:58,832 --> 00:30:00,533
NO, SINCE THE LAST GUYS LEFT
ABOUT A WEEK AGO.

665
00:30:05,103 --> 00:30:07,873
OH, NOW HE'S RUBBING
HIS RYAN O'NEALLY FACE

666
00:30:07,907 --> 00:30:10,777
ALL OVER HER'S.

667
00:30:10,810 --> 00:30:12,645
LET'S GET UP FIRST THING
IN THE MORNING.

668
00:30:12,678 --> 00:30:14,313
WE CAN HAVE
THE WHOLE DAY TOGETHER.

669
00:30:14,347 --> 00:30:16,215
I'LL WEAR MY GOAT'S HEAD,
IT'LL BE FUN.

670
00:30:16,248 --> 00:30:18,685
- [LAUGHS]
- WHAT'S SO FUNNY?

671
00:30:18,718 --> 00:30:21,720
YOU. YOU ARE.
COME ON, LET'S GO.

672
00:30:21,753 --> 00:30:23,222
PUT ON THE GLOVES,
GO SIX ROUNDS,

673
00:30:23,255 --> 00:30:25,192
SEE WHAT'RE MADE OF.
COME ON, LET'S GO!

674
00:30:28,562 --> 00:30:29,795
NIGHT, FISH.

675
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:32,432
[SERVO IMPERSONATES FISH]
GOOD NIGHT, KIDS.

676
00:30:37,437 --> 00:30:39,038
UH, JUST WANT TO DRIVE THROUGH

677
00:30:39,072 --> 00:30:41,040
THE DIRECTOR OF PHOTOGRAPHY
CREDIT REAL QUICK.

678
00:30:43,042 --> 00:30:44,210
YEAH.

679
00:30:44,243 --> 00:30:46,712
INSTANT BALL AND CHAIN,
I TELL YOU.

680
00:30:48,748 --> 00:30:51,383
GREAT BOLD ONES TONIGHT,
HUH, HONEY?

681
00:30:53,085 --> 00:30:55,053
DID YOU HAVE A NICE WALK?

682
00:30:55,087 --> 00:30:56,488
YES, MA'AM.

683
00:30:56,522 --> 00:30:58,725
UM, DON'T COME UP FOR
ABOUT FIVE MINUTES, OKAY?

684
00:31:00,527 --> 00:31:01,527
GOOD NIGHT.

685
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:04,663
[MAN YELLS ON TELEVISION]

686
00:31:04,697 --> 00:31:06,065
I SURE LOVE
THE YELLING CHANNEL.

687
00:31:10,570 --> 00:31:12,538
YOUR FOLKS SEEM
NICE AND EVIL.

688
00:31:15,408 --> 00:31:17,077
THAT'S YOUR ROOM.

689
00:31:17,110 --> 00:31:19,278
THERE'S TON OF VARNISHED BREAD
LAYING AROUND IN THERE.

690
00:31:19,312 --> 00:31:22,415
JUST PUSH IT OUT OF THE WAY.

691
00:31:22,448 --> 00:31:25,150
NICE DOOR. I'D LIKE TO SEE IT
CRUMPLED UP NEXT TO MY BED.

692
00:31:25,183 --> 00:31:27,620
OH, WAIT.

693
00:31:27,653 --> 00:31:30,757
RING ON MY DOOR
IN THE MORNING?

694
00:31:30,790 --> 00:31:33,492
- AT 6:00?
- SURE, WHY NOT?

695
00:31:33,525 --> 00:31:35,828
OKAY.

696
00:31:35,862 --> 00:31:37,997
WE'LL HAVE TO GET UP
AND MILK THE WALNUTS.

697
00:31:42,535 --> 00:31:44,837
GOOD NIGHT,
CREEPY VACUOUS GIRL.

698
00:31:49,708 --> 00:31:53,312
UH, SO I DON'T NEED A KISS
OR ANYTHING, I'M FINE.

699
00:31:56,715 --> 00:31:59,118
[SERVO HUMS]

700
00:31:59,152 --> 00:32:00,987
[SNIFFS]

701
00:32:01,020 --> 00:32:04,590
I LIKE TO SNIFF MY BLINDS
BEFORE I GO TO BED.

702
00:32:04,623 --> 00:32:07,393
HEY! BEELZEBUB, KALI,
AND LUCIFER.

703
00:32:12,898 --> 00:32:15,502
THEY GOT A SIGNED COPY
OF THE NECRONOMICON HERE.

704
00:32:15,535 --> 00:32:18,672
"YOU GUYS SCARE ME. HA, HA!
SIGNED, SATAN."

705
00:32:23,442 --> 00:32:25,578
AHH! IT'S A HIDEOUS THING
MADE OUT OF SKIN.

706
00:32:25,612 --> 00:32:27,680
OH, IT'S JUST ME.

707
00:32:30,350 --> 00:32:32,918
UH. THAT REPRESENTS
ALL MY HANG UPS, MAN.

708
00:32:32,952 --> 00:32:35,855
AND I JUST LET THEM FALL.

709
00:32:39,725 --> 00:32:41,760
HMM.

710
00:32:44,897 --> 00:32:47,367
EXCUSE ME,
I THINK I LEFT A SUSTACAL

711
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:49,835
BACK IN THE CORNER THERE.

712
00:32:49,868 --> 00:32:52,005
MUST GO AWAY.

713
00:32:52,038 --> 00:32:53,538
WHO ARE YOU?

714
00:32:53,572 --> 00:32:56,242
MY NAME IS
MARGARET RAWHIDE CHEW.

715
00:32:58,812 --> 00:33:00,880
I USUALLY LIKE
THE LEFT SIDE OF THE BED,

716
00:33:00,913 --> 00:33:02,182
IF THAT'S OKAY.

717
00:33:05,485 --> 00:33:07,453
HUH? DID A PLUCKED TURKEY

718
00:33:07,487 --> 00:33:08,888
IN A WIG JUST TALK TO ME?

719
00:33:17,730 --> 00:33:19,365
UH, FRONT DESK,

720
00:33:19,398 --> 00:33:21,733
THERE'S A MUMMY IN MY ROOM.

721
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:26,605
UH, MRS. ROTTEN PUMPKIN HEAD?
HELLO?

722
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:30,108
- WHO IS IT?
- IT'S ME.

723
00:33:30,142 --> 00:33:32,678
IS CAPTAIN HOOK THERE?

724
00:33:34,213 --> 00:33:35,648
GOT TO TALK TO YOU.

725
00:33:35,682 --> 00:33:37,283
YOU HAVE A NEEDLE? I NEED
TO RE-INFLATE YOUR GRANDMA.

726
00:33:40,285 --> 00:33:42,355
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

727
00:33:42,388 --> 00:33:45,123
IS THERE ANYBODY ELSE
IN THIS HOUSE
THAT I DON'T KNOW ABOUT?

728
00:33:45,157 --> 00:33:47,927
WELL, YOU KNOW ABOUT
MRS. WILMA "FAILED
GENETIC EXPERIMENT" RIGHT?

729
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,962
LUCINDA.

730
00:33:49,995 --> 00:33:52,465
SHE CAME RIGHT IN MY ROOM
AND SCARED THE HELL OUT OF ME.

731
00:33:52,498 --> 00:33:55,968
I'M SORRY
SHE FRIGHTENED YOU, JODIE.

732
00:33:56,002 --> 00:33:57,670
SHE ONLY KILLS
WHEN SHE'S CRAZY.

733
00:33:57,703 --> 00:33:59,605
BUT YOU MUSTN'T PAY
ANY ATTENTION TO HER.

734
00:33:59,638 --> 00:34:02,508
SHE'S AN OLD WOMAN AND SHE LIKES
TO WANDER AROUND THE HOUSE.

735
00:34:02,542 --> 00:34:04,943
IT WON'T HAPPEN AGAIN.

736
00:34:04,977 --> 00:34:06,512
WHO IS SHE?

737
00:34:06,545 --> 00:34:07,980
SHE'S MY GREAT GRANDMOTHER.

738
00:34:08,013 --> 00:34:09,382
SHE'S NOT THAT GREAT.

739
00:34:09,415 --> 00:34:11,683
WHAT HAPPENED TO HER FACE?

740
00:34:11,717 --> 00:34:14,053
WELL, SHE WAS BADLY BURNED
WHEN SHE WAS A YOUNG GIRL.

741
00:34:14,087 --> 00:34:15,488
THAT'S WHY--

742
00:34:15,522 --> 00:34:17,657
SHE DOESN'T GO OUT VERY MUCH
BECAUSE OF HER FACE.

743
00:34:17,690 --> 00:34:19,225
UNLESS SHE'S GOT
A COFFEE COUPON.

744
00:34:19,258 --> 00:34:21,027
GO BACK TO BED.

745
00:34:21,060 --> 00:34:23,328
SHE WAS JUST CURIOUS.

746
00:34:23,362 --> 00:34:25,565
I'LL GO TALK TO HER.

747
00:34:28,533 --> 00:34:31,537
OKAY.

748
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:33,172
OH, AND THERE'S
A HUGE, INSANE,

749
00:34:33,205 --> 00:34:34,907
SCABBY GORILLA
WANDERING AROUND, TOO.

750
00:34:34,940 --> 00:34:37,343
WHY DID SHE SAY,
"GO AWAY"?

751
00:34:37,377 --> 00:34:39,945
SHE'S AFRAID OF STRANGERS.

752
00:34:39,978 --> 00:34:42,615
WELL, SHE WASN'T AFRAID TO COME
INTO MY ROOM WITHOUT KNOCKING.

753
00:34:42,648 --> 00:34:44,950
SHE'S AN OLD LADY, JODIE.

754
00:34:44,983 --> 00:34:47,287
THEY DON'T KNOW WHAT THEY'RE
DOING HALF THE TIME.

755
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:49,555
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT, I'LL GO
FLIP HER LEFT TURN SIGNAL ON,

756
00:34:49,588 --> 00:34:50,957
AND SHE'LL GO
RIGHT BACK TO SLEEP.

757
00:34:50,990 --> 00:34:53,292
I'M SORRY.

758
00:34:53,325 --> 00:34:54,793
GO BACK TO BED.

759
00:34:54,827 --> 00:34:56,895
UH, COULD YOU MAKE
YOUR GRANDMA WEAR A BELL?

760
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:59,665
OKAY.

761
00:35:10,943 --> 00:35:13,545
I'M GONNA LOCK THE DOOR NOW.

762
00:35:13,578 --> 00:35:15,113
DO YOU UNDERSTAND?

763
00:35:15,147 --> 00:35:17,783
I HAVEN'T UNDERSTOOD ANYTHING
SINCE McKINLEY WENT DOWN.

764
00:35:17,817 --> 00:35:20,285
[MUTTERS]

765
00:35:20,318 --> 00:35:22,822
SHE'S SAYING, "NEVER TRY
TO DEEP-FRY A SNOWBALL."

766
00:35:22,855 --> 00:35:25,792
NO, NO, IT'S LATE.

767
00:35:25,825 --> 00:35:28,060
YOU HAVE TO GO TO SLEEP NOW.

768
00:35:28,093 --> 00:35:29,562
[MUTTERS]

769
00:35:29,595 --> 00:35:32,465
TOMORROW, I'LL TAKE YOU
FOR AN EXTRA-LONG WALK.

770
00:35:32,498 --> 00:35:35,300
ALL THE WAY TO THE DRESSING
TABLE AND BACK.

771
00:35:39,172 --> 00:35:40,372
YOU KNOW, THERE'S
A DELIGHTFUL SCENE

772
00:35:40,405 --> 00:35:44,010
LATER IN THE MOVIE WHERE
THIS OLD WOMAN RAPS.

773
00:35:44,043 --> 00:35:45,477
NO, THERE ISN'T.

774
00:35:45,512 --> 00:35:47,180
GOOD NIGHT.

775
00:35:47,213 --> 00:35:49,848
- AND BY "GOOD NIGHT,"
I MEAN "SHUT UP.
- ...MY SISTER.

776
00:35:56,188 --> 00:35:58,557
I JUST WANTED TO GIVE HER
A WERTHERS.

777
00:36:01,727 --> 00:36:04,663
OH MAN, NOW A WITHERED OLD
BILLY ZANE IS GONNA COME IN

778
00:36:04,697 --> 00:36:07,267
AND GIVE HER A WITHERED OLD
COEUR DE LA MER.

779
00:36:09,568 --> 00:36:11,303
[SERVO SIGHS] AH, GOOD DAY.

780
00:36:11,337 --> 00:36:13,072
TOOK A WALK.
GOT THAT DRESS SEWN.

781
00:36:13,105 --> 00:36:14,940
KILLED.

782
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:26,052
A WRINKLE!

783
00:36:26,085 --> 00:36:28,853
HUH, WELL, IT'S KIND OF
A LATERAL MOVE, ACTUALLY.

784
00:36:30,757 --> 00:36:34,327
SHE TURNED INTO
CECILIA BARTOLI.

785
00:36:34,360 --> 00:36:37,095
I MISS MY EDDIE MUNSTER
WIDOW'S PEAK.

786
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:48,640
I STILL GOTTA WORK
ON THE MUSTACHE, THOUGH.

787
00:36:48,673 --> 00:36:51,243
AH, BACK TO BEING
SWIFTY LAZAR.

788
00:36:52,978 --> 00:36:56,248
WHO'S GOT IT GOING ON?
ME, THAT'S WHO.

789
00:36:56,282 --> 00:36:59,552
WHAT ELSE ARE WE GOING
TO DO TODAY?

790
00:36:59,585 --> 00:37:00,787
WOULD YOU MIND
DRIVING ME TO TOWN

791
00:37:00,820 --> 00:37:02,455
SO I CAN GO TO THE STORE?

792
00:37:02,488 --> 00:37:05,223
- SURE.
- AH, MY PET TICK.

793
00:37:05,257 --> 00:37:07,158
I'LL GO CHANGE AND TELL THEM
WE'RE LEAVING.

794
00:37:07,192 --> 00:37:08,493
- MEET ME AT THE CAR.
- OKAY.

795
00:37:08,527 --> 00:37:12,332
AAY, I GOT ROOKED.

796
00:37:12,365 --> 00:37:14,000
MY CUP'S GLUED TO MY LIP.

797
00:37:16,702 --> 00:37:20,740
MOM LOOKS LIKE RON POPEIL.

798
00:37:20,773 --> 00:37:23,442
I ASKED JODIE TO STAY
A FEW DAYS, AND HE AGREED.

799
00:37:23,475 --> 00:37:24,677
HE AGREED THAT
SHE ASKED HIM?

800
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:26,145
FIGURED YOU WOULD.

801
00:37:28,813 --> 00:37:31,750
JODIE'S GONNA DRIVE ME
TO THE STORE.

802
00:37:31,783 --> 00:37:33,953
DOES HE KNOW
EVERYTHING WE NEED?

803
00:37:33,987 --> 00:37:36,822
- YES.
- WE'LL PROBABLY STOP BY
WHERE THE FISH LIVES.

804
00:37:40,660 --> 00:37:43,362
I SAID JODIE'S AGREED
TO STAY A FEW DAYS.

805
00:37:43,395 --> 00:37:45,263
WE HEARD YOU THE FIRST TIME.

806
00:37:45,297 --> 00:37:47,232
WE WEREN'T INTERESTED
THEN EITHER.

807
00:37:49,602 --> 00:37:52,137
AND IT'S ALL RIGHT WITH YOU?

808
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:53,805
NO, IT'S NOT
ALL RIGHT WITH ME,

809
00:37:53,838 --> 00:37:55,975
BUT IT'S YOUR DECISION,
NOT MINE.

810
00:37:56,008 --> 00:37:58,310
UH, MIKE, IF YOU'RE EVER
THIS FAMILY'S SECRET SANTA,

811
00:37:58,343 --> 00:38:01,547
DON'T BUY THEM POTHOLDERS.

812
00:38:01,580 --> 00:38:03,482
THAT MEANS A GREAT DEAL
TO ME, LUTHER.

813
00:38:03,515 --> 00:38:05,083
I MEAN, "MR. VANDROSS."

814
00:38:08,220 --> 00:38:09,588
THANK YOU.

815
00:38:09,622 --> 00:38:13,025
♪ IS THIS THE LITTLE DEMON
I CARRIED? ♪

816
00:38:13,058 --> 00:38:15,027
GO TO THE STORE.

817
00:38:15,060 --> 00:38:18,530
BUY CANNED PEACHES
AND DISHWASHING LIQUID.

818
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:26,705
I SHOULD STOP
DYING MY EYEBROWS.

819
00:38:26,738 --> 00:38:29,442
- MELISSA?
- HUH?

820
00:38:29,475 --> 00:38:31,177
WHAT ARE YOU GONNA TELL HIM?

821
00:38:31,210 --> 00:38:33,712
I DON'T KNOW.

822
00:38:33,745 --> 00:38:37,517
I'LL HAVE TO WAIT AND SEE.

823
00:38:37,550 --> 00:38:40,452
MIKING HER SHOE BOTTOMS?

824
00:38:40,485 --> 00:38:43,288
WELL, TIME TO STICK MY CUP
BACK IN MY LIPS.

825
00:38:47,493 --> 00:38:50,262
OH YEAH, HE'S A HOT ONE,
ALL RIGHT.

826
00:38:50,295 --> 00:38:52,398
OH, AND THEY DON'T NEED
PLANT HOLDERS EITHER, MIKE.

827
00:38:52,432 --> 00:38:54,100
I MEAN, YOU KNOW, IF YOU'RE
THEIR SECRET SANTA.

828
00:38:54,133 --> 00:38:56,635
GOT IT.

829
00:38:56,668 --> 00:38:59,272
WELL, OFF TO MY
STEWARDESS JOB.

830
00:38:59,305 --> 00:39:00,840
YOU READY TO GO?

831
00:39:00,873 --> 00:39:03,408
YEAH, LET'S GO.

832
00:39:03,442 --> 00:39:05,010
TAKE A LEFT RIGHT THERE.

833
00:39:05,043 --> 00:39:07,012
GOOD.

834
00:39:09,515 --> 00:39:11,650
LOOK OUT! WALNUT STAMPEDE!

835
00:39:13,552 --> 00:39:15,487
HEY, WANNA PLAY
PITCHFORK BUG?

836
00:39:18,523 --> 00:39:20,325
WELL NOW, ANDY, I THINK

837
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:22,060
THERE WAS A DEMON
IN THE CAR!

838
00:39:25,998 --> 00:39:28,100
ENHANCE YOUR MOODY
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC

839
00:39:28,133 --> 00:39:31,470
WITH TINY FART SOUNDS.

840
00:39:31,503 --> 00:39:34,973
[ALL MAKE FART SOUNDS]

841
00:39:35,007 --> 00:39:37,677
HE'S GOT TWO HUGE SUDAFED
ON TOP OF HIS CAR.

842
00:39:39,645 --> 00:39:42,715
- SEE?
- [MORE FART SOUNDS]

843
00:39:51,090 --> 00:39:52,658
HUH. FROM THE WAIST DOWN,

844
00:39:52,692 --> 00:39:56,328
A WOMAN.

845
00:39:56,362 --> 00:39:59,098
MAN, I TRY TO KEEP FIT,
BUT AFTER THE THIRD BABY.

846
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:04,370
UM, HI, YOU SEEN THE OTHER
VILLAGE PEOPLE?

847
00:40:06,738 --> 00:40:08,940
BOY, THAT BODY PILE'S
REALLY GROWING.

848
00:40:08,973 --> 00:40:10,242
OH, THAT GRANDMA.

849
00:40:13,645 --> 00:40:15,882
DIE DIE DIE!
I MEAN-- HELLO.

850
00:40:15,915 --> 00:40:17,617
- WELL, HELLO, MR. MASON.
- HOWDY, MRS. STRICKLAND.

851
00:40:17,650 --> 00:40:21,353
- LUTHER AROUND?
- I BELIEVE HE'S AROUND
IN THE BACK.

852
00:40:21,387 --> 00:40:22,688
YOU MIND IF I WIND UP
BACK THERE?

853
00:40:22,722 --> 00:40:24,123
- OF COURSE NOT.
- THANK YOU, MA'AM.

854
00:40:24,157 --> 00:40:26,792
HE'S GOT A REAL WALNUT JONES
TODAY, MAN.

855
00:40:26,825 --> 00:40:29,128
THERE'S NOT ANYTHING
WRONG, I HOPE.

856
00:40:29,162 --> 00:40:30,963
OH NO, MRS. STRICKLAND,
I JUST WANNA

857
00:40:30,997 --> 00:40:32,598
CHEW THE FAT WITH LUTHER
FOR A WHILE.

858
00:40:32,632 --> 00:40:33,965
I'LL BE SEEING YOU.

859
00:40:33,998 --> 00:40:37,903
HE EVEN BROUGHT HIS OWN FAT.

860
00:40:37,937 --> 00:40:40,305
HMM, WOULD HE EVEN FIT
IN THE IRON MAIDEN?

861
00:40:42,107 --> 00:40:44,477
WELL, HELLO, JOHN.
WHAT BRINGS YOU OUT THIS WAY?

862
00:40:44,510 --> 00:40:47,245
AND IF YOU SAY "MY SQUAD CAR,"
I'LL CHAINSAW YOU IN HALF.

863
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:50,315
OH, NOTHING MUCH,
JUST KIND OF POKING AROUND.

864
00:40:50,348 --> 00:40:52,885
- SIT DOWN, TAKE A LOAD OFF.
- THANK YOU.

865
00:40:52,918 --> 00:40:54,587
GOT THE KETTLE OF HANDS
GOING, I SEE.

866
00:40:57,823 --> 00:41:00,258
LUTHER, DOESN'T THE BACK
OF YOUR PLACE BUTT UP AGAINST

867
00:41:00,292 --> 00:41:02,928
- OLD MAN LARSEN'S PROPERTY?
- MM-HMM, SURE IT DOES.

868
00:41:02,962 --> 00:41:05,330
YOU DON'T MIND IF I CHEW
ON THIS STICK INSECT, DO YOU?

869
00:41:05,363 --> 00:41:08,500
YOU STILL WORKING
ON THAT LARSEN BUSINESS?

870
00:41:08,533 --> 00:41:10,635
HARRIS TOMLEY STILL
GOT HIS WIND UP.

871
00:41:10,668 --> 00:41:12,303
THINKS IF WE CAN
BREAK THIS THING,

872
00:41:12,337 --> 00:41:14,973
HE'LL BE RE-ELECTED SHERIFF
FOR THE NEXT 20 YEARS.

873
00:41:15,007 --> 00:41:16,775
DAMN FOOL.

874
00:41:16,808 --> 00:41:18,110
HE'S RUNNING AROUND
OVER IN NEWPORT

875
00:41:18,143 --> 00:41:19,345
LIKE HE THOUGHT HE WAS
J. EDGAR HOOVER.

876
00:41:19,378 --> 00:41:21,013
PRETTY DRESS, THOUGH.

877
00:41:21,047 --> 00:41:23,048
- HOW CAN I HELP?
- HEH.

878
00:41:25,083 --> 00:41:27,620
YOU MIND IF I JUST
TAKE A LOOK AROUND YOUR PLACE?

879
00:41:27,653 --> 00:41:29,188
'COURSE NOT.

880
00:41:29,222 --> 00:41:30,688
WHAT'RE YOU LOOKING FOR?

881
00:41:30,722 --> 00:41:33,392
HELL, I DON'T KNOW.
AIN'T FOUND NOTHING YET.

882
00:41:33,425 --> 00:41:35,827
NOT EVEN A SUSPICIOUS-LOOKING
COW CHIP.

883
00:41:35,862 --> 00:41:38,130
- OOH.
- LOOKS LIKE WHOEVER
KILLED THE OLD MAN

884
00:41:38,163 --> 00:41:39,498
WENT UP IN A PUFF OF SMOKE.

885
00:41:39,532 --> 00:41:41,467
I SEE.

886
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:43,502
SO YOU DON'T HAVE ANY IDEA
AT ALL WHO MIGHT'VE DONE IT?

887
00:41:43,535 --> 00:41:45,203
NO, NOTHING.

888
00:41:45,237 --> 00:41:47,973
THAT'S WHY WE'RE ALL
JUST OUT, POKING AROUND.

889
00:41:48,007 --> 00:41:49,642
I GUESS THE SHERIFF
HOPES WE'LL FIND

890
00:41:49,675 --> 00:41:51,710
A SIGNED CONFESSION
JUST LAYING IN THE GRASS.

891
00:41:51,743 --> 00:41:54,380
WELL, HELP YOURSELF
TO MY PLACE, JOHN.

892
00:41:54,413 --> 00:41:55,882
TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU WANT.

893
00:41:55,915 --> 00:41:58,517
JUST DON'T
SPOOK THE WALNUTS.

894
00:41:58,550 --> 00:42:01,687
THANKS A LOT, LUTHER.
I APPRECIATE THAT.

895
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:03,888
- LISTEN.
- MY TUMMY'S GROWLIN'.

896
00:42:03,922 --> 00:42:06,258
WHEN YOU GET THROUGH POKING
AROUND, COME ON UP TO THE HOUSE.

897
00:42:06,292 --> 00:42:08,560
WE'LL HAVE A TOUCH
OF MY CIDER.

898
00:42:08,593 --> 00:42:10,595
I KNEW YOU WERE
GONNA SAY THAT, LUTHER.

899
00:42:10,628 --> 00:42:12,230
THEN GIVE ME THE FINGER
LIKE THAT.

900
00:42:12,263 --> 00:42:16,035
BUT IF SHERIFF TOMMY FINDS OUT
I WAS DRINKING YOUR CIDER,

901
00:42:16,068 --> 00:42:18,570
I MAY HAVE TO START
WORKING FOR A LIVING.

902
00:42:18,603 --> 00:42:20,572
THANKS ANYWAY, LUTHER,
I'LL SEE YOU IN TEN.

903
00:42:22,808 --> 00:42:25,077
BY THE WAY, THERE'S NO REASON
TO LOOK IN THE CRAWLSPACE.

904
00:42:25,110 --> 00:42:27,613
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

905
00:42:29,248 --> 00:42:30,615
SHE'S GONNA GO BUY
A WHOLE BUNCH

906
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:34,587
OF PROCTER & GAMBLE
PRODUCTS.

907
00:42:34,620 --> 00:42:35,955
WHY DO I SUDDENLY
FEEL HUNGRY

908
00:42:35,988 --> 00:42:39,492
FOR CARNATION ICE CREAM?

909
00:42:39,525 --> 00:42:43,262
I LIKE THIS PLACE BECAUSE
THEY HAVE BULK EYE OF NEWT.

910
00:42:43,295 --> 00:42:45,130
TWO, THREE.

911
00:42:45,163 --> 00:42:49,000
AND THEN-- GET THIS-- FOUR!

912
00:42:49,033 --> 00:42:50,835
MORNING, MR. GENTRY.

913
00:42:50,868 --> 00:42:52,070
HELLO, MELISSA.

914
00:42:52,103 --> 00:42:53,738
PLEASE FEEL FREE
TO PERUSE MY SUPPLY

915
00:42:53,772 --> 00:42:55,340
OF UNGUENTS, SUSPENSIONS,

916
00:42:55,373 --> 00:42:57,408
TINCTURES,
COMPOUNDED FORMULAS,

917
00:42:57,442 --> 00:43:00,145
AND OTHER SUNDRIES.

918
00:43:00,178 --> 00:43:01,847
EH, ANYWAY,

919
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:03,615
I WILL SHAKE THE PAINT
OFF YOUR WALLS, HONEY.

920
00:43:07,887 --> 00:43:09,087
WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH THESE PEOPLE?

921
00:43:09,120 --> 00:43:10,655
YOU'D THINK WE HAVE
THE PLAGUE OR SOMETHING.

922
00:43:10,688 --> 00:43:12,792
IT'S NOT YOU, IT'S JUST ME.

923
00:43:12,825 --> 00:43:15,027
YEP, GOT THE PLAGUE.
WANNA MAKE OUT?

924
00:43:15,060 --> 00:43:16,895
THEY ALWAYS BEHAVE THAT WAY.

925
00:43:16,928 --> 00:43:19,632
WELL, WHY?

926
00:43:19,665 --> 00:43:22,333
THEY SAY IN THIS TOWN
THAT I'M A WITCH.

927
00:43:22,367 --> 00:43:23,802
[LAUGHS] A WITCH.

928
00:43:23,835 --> 00:43:26,072
IT ONLY RHYMES WITH "WITCH."

929
00:43:29,442 --> 00:43:31,710
OH, YOU PLAGUE-RIDDEN
LITTLE WITCH.

930
00:43:34,413 --> 00:43:36,382
HERE.

931
00:43:36,415 --> 00:43:37,917
SEE WHAT I MEAN?

932
00:43:37,950 --> 00:43:41,687
WITCHES CAN'T LIFT FLOUR
ON THEIR OWN.

933
00:43:41,720 --> 00:43:43,922
WHY DO THEY THINK
YOU'RE A WITCH?

934
00:43:43,955 --> 00:43:45,757
BECAUSE I AM.

935
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,058
AH, STOP IT.

936
00:43:47,092 --> 00:43:50,528
YOU DON'T BELIEVE ME?
ASK 'EM.

937
00:43:50,562 --> 00:43:51,930
SHE GIVES THEM $15.55

938
00:43:51,963 --> 00:43:54,700
JUST SO SHE CAN GET
$6.66 BACK IN CHANGE.

939
00:43:58,270 --> 00:43:59,605
THIS IS A TENSE MOMENT

940
00:43:59,638 --> 00:44:01,440
BECAUSE SHE USED
TO DATE THE GROCER.

941
00:44:01,473 --> 00:44:04,577
THANK YOU, MELISSA.

942
00:44:04,610 --> 00:44:05,877
- YOU'RE WELCOME.
- THEN YOU'LL JUST

943
00:44:05,910 --> 00:44:08,213
DELIVER THE BROOMSTICKS
TO MY HOUSE.

944
00:44:11,250 --> 00:44:13,218
HEY, THEY GOT A SALE
ON MISMATCHED BEER.

945
00:44:13,252 --> 00:44:15,653
MM. STEINLAGER. PETE'S.

946
00:44:18,457 --> 00:44:19,792
ZAH!

947
00:44:19,825 --> 00:44:22,995
AH, YOU MADE ME GO BURPY.

948
00:44:23,028 --> 00:44:25,230
[CHUCKLES] I SAID "ZAH."

949
00:44:25,263 --> 00:44:26,965
- YOUNG WHIPPERSNAPPER.
- WHERE'S HE FROM?

950
00:44:26,998 --> 00:44:29,167
THE GROCER'S WIFE DIED
WHEN SOMEONE SAID "ZAH."

951
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,435
IT'S NOT FUNNY.

952
00:44:30,468 --> 00:44:33,105
- WHY'D YOU DO THAT?
- SERVES THEM RIGHT.

953
00:44:33,138 --> 00:44:36,175
YOU JUST MADE IT WORSE,
DOING A SILLY THING LIKE THAT.

954
00:44:36,208 --> 00:44:39,143
I'M SORRY, MELISSA, BUT THAT
SORT OF THING BUGS ME.

955
00:44:39,177 --> 00:44:41,580
COME ON, LET'S GO.

956
00:44:41,613 --> 00:44:44,650
I'VE SAID "ZAH"
IN BETTER TOWNS THAN THIS.

957
00:44:44,683 --> 00:44:46,352
AFTER THE MOVIE,
REMEMBER TO PICK UP

958
00:44:46,385 --> 00:44:49,688
SOME CARNATION ICE CREAM!

959
00:44:57,662 --> 00:44:59,665
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

960
00:44:59,698 --> 00:45:00,965
ANYTHING?

961
00:45:00,998 --> 00:45:03,635
HMM. HMM.

962
00:45:03,668 --> 00:45:05,337
NOPE, NOPE, NOPE,
I'M FINE, MIKE.

963
00:45:05,370 --> 00:45:07,472
I GUESS ALL WE CAN DO
IS ADD MORE ROCKS.

964
00:45:07,505 --> 00:45:09,442
OKAY.

965
00:45:09,475 --> 00:45:11,008
YOU KNOW, I'M WORRIED.

966
00:45:11,042 --> 00:45:13,178
IF I WASN'T A WITCH,
I'D BE DEAD BY NOW

967
00:45:13,212 --> 00:45:14,813
OR AT LEAST SHRIEKING OUT
A CONFESSION

968
00:45:14,847 --> 00:45:17,148
OR RAINING DOWN CURSES
ON MY TORMENTORS.

969
00:45:17,182 --> 00:45:19,117
BUT INSTEAD,
HEY, I'M GREAT.

970
00:45:19,150 --> 00:45:20,185
I COULDN'T BE BETTER.

971
00:45:20,218 --> 00:45:22,153
AH. OKAY.

972
00:45:22,187 --> 00:45:23,655
ANYTHING?

973
00:45:23,688 --> 00:45:26,225
OH, NO, DID YOU
ACTUALLY ADD ONE?

974
00:45:26,258 --> 00:45:28,360
NO, I'M FINE.
VERY COMFORTABLE IN FACT.

975
00:45:28,393 --> 00:45:29,662
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

976
00:45:29,695 --> 00:45:31,062
YEAH, CROW,
WHAT I DON'T GET IS,

977
00:45:31,097 --> 00:45:32,865
WHY DO YOU ASSUME YOU'RE
A WITCH IN THE FIRST PLACE?

978
00:45:32,898 --> 00:45:34,365
WELL, I DON'T REALLY
ASSUME IT, MIKE,

979
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,168
BUT I GUESS IT'S ALWAYS BEEN
IN THE BACK OF MY MIND.

980
00:45:36,202 --> 00:45:37,702
- YOU KNOW?
- HMM, YEAH.

981
00:45:37,735 --> 00:45:40,038
WELL, YOU KNOW, CROW, THE REASON
YOU CAN SURVIVE ALL OF THIS

982
00:45:40,072 --> 00:45:43,008
IS BECAUSE OF YOUR DURABLE
MOLYBDENUM FRAME.

983
00:45:43,042 --> 00:45:44,843
WELL, THAT'S NICE OF YOU
TO SAY, MIKE.

984
00:45:44,877 --> 00:45:46,378
BUT LET'S FACE IT,
I'M A WITCH.

985
00:45:46,412 --> 00:45:48,213
YOU MIGHT AS WELL
BURN ME AT THE STAKE.

986
00:45:48,247 --> 00:45:50,448
OH, CROW,
YOU'RE NOT A WITCH.

987
00:45:50,482 --> 00:45:51,783
BUT, YOU KNOW,
IT IS HARD FOR ME

988
00:45:51,817 --> 00:45:54,052
TO PROVE A NEGATIVE,
YOU KNOW?

989
00:45:54,085 --> 00:45:56,955
I CAN'T REALLY PROVE YOU'RE
NOT A FROG, FOR INSTANCE.

990
00:45:56,988 --> 00:45:59,223
MIKE, THIS IS WEIRD.

991
00:45:59,257 --> 00:46:01,360
OH, WHAT, YOU FEELING
SOME PAIN? IS IT WORKING?

992
00:46:01,393 --> 00:46:03,328
NO, HOW'D YOU KNOW I WAS
THINKING I MIGHT BE A FROG?

993
00:46:03,362 --> 00:46:04,630
DID I TELL YOU THAT?

994
00:46:04,663 --> 00:46:06,398
NO, I MEAN, I JUST
USED IT AS AN EXAMPLE--

995
00:46:06,432 --> 00:46:08,200
RIBBIT. I'M A FROG! RIBBIT.

996
00:46:08,233 --> 00:46:10,102
I'M A FROG--
GET THESE ROCKS OFF ME.

997
00:46:10,135 --> 00:46:12,070
I CAN'T STAND THIS KIND OF
WEIGHT, I'M A TINY FROG!

998
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:13,272
- NO, YOU'RE NOT A FROG.
- [ALARM BLARES]

999
00:46:13,305 --> 00:46:14,740
HEY, YOU GUYS,
WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

1000
00:46:14,773 --> 00:46:16,073
OH, WELL, HELP ME
WITH THESE ROCKS.

1001
00:46:16,107 --> 00:46:17,275
OKAY-- WHOA!

1002
00:46:17,308 --> 00:46:18,777
YOU KNOW WHAT THIS MEANS?
I'M NOT A WITCH!

1003
00:46:18,810 --> 00:46:20,945
I'M A FROG!

1004
00:46:30,688 --> 00:46:32,623
- SORRY ABOUT THAT.
- YOU DO BELIEVE YOU'RE
A WITCH, DON'T YOU?

1005
00:46:32,657 --> 00:46:33,925
NO, I'M A FROG.

1006
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,127
OH, WE'RE BACK HERE
AT THE MOVIE.

1007
00:46:35,160 --> 00:46:36,962
YES.

1008
00:46:36,995 --> 00:46:38,997
THERE'S NO SUCH THING
AS WITCHES.

1009
00:46:39,030 --> 00:46:40,632
I MEAN REAL WITCHES.

1010
00:46:40,665 --> 00:46:43,002
REAL WITCHES.

1011
00:46:43,035 --> 00:46:44,937
YEAH, YOU KNOW.

1012
00:46:44,970 --> 00:46:47,638
THE KIND THEY BURN.

1013
00:46:47,672 --> 00:46:51,343
YOU ARE SO WITCHIST.

1014
00:46:51,377 --> 00:46:54,513
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

1015
00:46:54,547 --> 00:46:56,348
WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE
WHERE I DO MY WITCHCRAFT?

1016
00:46:56,382 --> 00:46:59,050
I DO IT OUT OF KINKO'S.

1017
00:46:59,083 --> 00:47:00,518
YEAH, I GUESS SO.

1018
00:47:00,552 --> 00:47:03,888
OKAY, I'LL SHOW YOU
WHERE TO TURN.

1019
00:47:03,922 --> 00:47:05,490
I'M JUST GONNA
STOP AT THIS FARM

1020
00:47:05,523 --> 00:47:08,460
AND SAY "ZAH"
TO SOMEBODY, OKAY?

1021
00:47:08,493 --> 00:47:11,797
[SERVO HUMS WITH MUSIC]

1022
00:47:11,830 --> 00:47:14,900
UH-OH, THIS SCENE'S GONNA
PLAY HELL ON MY HAY FEVER.

1023
00:47:14,933 --> 00:47:17,002
- THIS IS IT.
- [SERVO SNEEZES]

1024
00:47:17,035 --> 00:47:19,203
- WOW.
- IT DOESN'T LOOK
VERY FORBIDDING.

1025
00:47:19,237 --> 00:47:20,738
[SERVO SNEEZES]

1026
00:47:20,772 --> 00:47:22,673
WHY SHOULD IT BE FORBIDDING?

1027
00:47:22,707 --> 00:47:25,877
WELL, IF THIS IS WHERE YOU
DO YOUR WITCHCRAFT--

1028
00:47:25,910 --> 00:47:27,913
- [SERVO SNEEZES]
- WOW.
- JEEZ.

1029
00:47:27,947 --> 00:47:30,015
JUST WHAT KIND OF WITCHCRAFT
DO YOU DO?

1030
00:47:30,048 --> 00:47:31,850
[SERVO SNEEZES, SNIFFLES]

1031
00:47:31,883 --> 00:47:34,987
OH, I WITCH THE BIRDS
INTO SINGING

1032
00:47:35,020 --> 00:47:38,357
- AND THE SUN INTO COMING OUT.
- YOU ALL RIGHT?

1033
00:47:38,390 --> 00:47:39,925
MAKING EVERYTHING

1034
00:47:39,958 --> 00:47:42,427
LOOK THE WAY IT LOOKS.

1035
00:47:42,460 --> 00:47:44,028
YOU'RE A VERY LOVELY WITCH.

1036
00:47:44,062 --> 00:47:46,898
WITH YOUR SOFT DOWNY WARTS.

1037
00:47:46,932 --> 00:47:50,302
COME ON.

1038
00:47:50,335 --> 00:47:52,603
CABIN FIVE IS NOT
ON THE LAKE, PER SE.

1039
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:56,542
YOU KNOW, IF SHE HAD
ANOTHER ONE OF THESE,

1040
00:47:56,575 --> 00:47:58,743
SHE COULD BE MELISSA
"TWO SHEDS" STRICKLAND.

1041
00:47:58,777 --> 00:48:00,612
[MIKE LAUGHS]

1042
00:48:03,515 --> 00:48:05,383
TAKE A LOOK INSIDE.

1043
00:48:05,417 --> 00:48:06,952
JUST WALK INTO
THE SPINNING BLADES.

1044
00:48:06,985 --> 00:48:08,653
IT'S NICE.

1045
00:48:12,757 --> 00:48:14,325
WAIT, YOU CAN'T USE
"AMAZING GRACE"

1046
00:48:14,358 --> 00:48:16,628
IN A DEVIL MOVIE!

1047
00:48:16,662 --> 00:48:20,065
- GO ON IN.
- OKAY.

1048
00:48:20,098 --> 00:48:22,033
OOH, LOTS OF PIG HEADS.

1049
00:48:24,468 --> 00:48:26,772
OH, SHE'S A TALENT AGENT
FOR THE MORMONS.

1050
00:48:30,175 --> 00:48:32,843
YOUR OWN PLACE.

1051
00:48:32,877 --> 00:48:34,478
UH, SORRY, THAT'S
THE MOST INTERESTING THING

1052
00:48:34,512 --> 00:48:36,147
I COULD COME UP WITH.

1053
00:48:36,180 --> 00:48:37,983
COME IN HERE
AND SHUT THE DOOR

1054
00:48:38,017 --> 00:48:41,420
AND LEAVE THE WORLD
OUT THERE SOMEWHERE.

1055
00:48:41,453 --> 00:48:43,988
DO YOU LIKE TO TURN OFF
THE WORLD SOMETIMES?

1056
00:48:44,022 --> 00:48:46,692
NO. NO, I'M AFRAID
I MIGHT MISS SOMETHING.

1057
00:48:46,725 --> 00:48:49,628
OH, HE TURNS OFF
THE WORLD, ALL RIGHT.

1058
00:48:49,662 --> 00:48:51,797
YOU DO, THOUGH, DON'T YOU?

1059
00:48:51,830 --> 00:48:54,365
YES. SOMETIMES.

1060
00:48:54,398 --> 00:48:58,203
MOSTLY I JUST LIKE
TO TURN OFF CANADA.

1061
00:48:58,237 --> 00:49:00,405
- WELL?
- SHALL WE TRADE CLOTHES?

1062
00:49:00,438 --> 00:49:01,640
WELL WHAT?

1063
00:49:01,673 --> 00:49:03,975
WELL, DO SOME WITCH THINGS.

1064
00:49:04,008 --> 00:49:06,345
WHAT WOULD YOU
LIKE ME TO DO?

1065
00:49:06,378 --> 00:49:07,745
UM, MAKE ME DISAPPEAR.

1066
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,213
YAY!

1067
00:49:09,247 --> 00:49:11,248
I WOULDN'T LIKE TO DO THAT.

1068
00:49:11,282 --> 00:49:12,917
MAKE SOMEBODY APPEAR, THEN.

1069
00:49:16,287 --> 00:49:17,788
THERE'S BEEN
A WALNUT UPRISING.

1070
00:49:20,458 --> 00:49:22,027
HELLO THERE.

1071
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:25,163
I MUST AGREE WITH THAT.

1072
00:49:25,197 --> 00:49:28,567
IS LUCINDA OUT AGAIN?

1073
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:30,435
SHE WANDERED INTO
JODIE'S ROOM LAST NIGHT.

1074
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:32,770
SCARED HIM HALF TO DEATH.

1075
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:36,007
WE'LL HELP YOU LOOK FOR HER.

1076
00:49:36,040 --> 00:49:38,043
YOU-- YOU STAY HERE.

1077
00:49:38,077 --> 00:49:39,878
STAY HERE.

1078
00:49:39,912 --> 00:49:41,413
HAVE A GOOD TIME.

1079
00:49:41,447 --> 00:49:44,282
HAVE SOME TOAST
OR SOMETHING.

1080
00:49:44,315 --> 00:49:46,283
POOR LUCINDA.

1081
00:49:46,317 --> 00:49:49,053
I'M THE ONLY ONE SHE
FEELS COMFORTABLE WITH.

1082
00:49:49,087 --> 00:49:51,122
EXCEPT HER DOLL.

1083
00:49:51,155 --> 00:49:52,390
MM.

1084
00:49:52,423 --> 00:49:55,227
SAD. IT REALLY IS.

1085
00:49:55,260 --> 00:49:57,062
YEP. REALLY, REALLY,
REALLY SAD.

1086
00:49:57,095 --> 00:49:59,630
- OKAY, SEX THEN?
- WHAT'S IN THE CHEST?

1087
00:49:59,663 --> 00:50:01,400
BEG YOUR PARDON?

1088
00:50:01,433 --> 00:50:03,000
I'LL SHOW YOU.

1089
00:50:09,307 --> 00:50:11,610
WELL, HEY, A FROG
THAT'S NOT DEFORMED.

1090
00:50:16,782 --> 00:50:18,983
HUH, YOUR MAVERICK
IS ROLLING DOWN THE HILL.

1091
00:50:20,885 --> 00:50:23,655
WOO, THE SUN JUST
GO NOVA OUT THERE?

1092
00:50:26,323 --> 00:50:27,758
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

1093
00:50:27,792 --> 00:50:29,995
I CAN'T TAKE
THE PACE ANYMORE.

1094
00:50:30,028 --> 00:50:32,797
I'M NOT SURE.

1095
00:50:32,830 --> 00:50:36,200
- WILL YOU TAKE ME
HOME, PLEASE?
- SURE.

1096
00:50:36,233 --> 00:50:38,470
STILL, THAT WAS ONE OF
THE SNAPPIEST CONVERSATIONS

1097
00:50:38,503 --> 00:50:40,472
- THEY'VE HAD YET.
- MM-HMM.

1098
00:50:44,342 --> 00:50:47,478
WELP, OBVIOUSLY A HERD
OF GRANDMAS CAME THROUGH HERE.

1099
00:50:54,920 --> 00:50:57,422
AH-HAH, I FOUND
THE MURDER WEAPON.

1100
00:51:02,393 --> 00:51:03,795
I'M GETTING WAY AHEAD
OF EVERYONE

1101
00:51:03,828 --> 00:51:05,730
ON THIS SCAVENGER HUNT.

1102
00:51:10,602 --> 00:51:12,070
HEY, A GIANT MATCHSTICK.

1103
00:51:12,103 --> 00:51:14,238
I COULD CHEW ON THIS
FOR MONTHS!

1104
00:51:18,743 --> 00:51:21,547
UH, I THOUGHT OF A SECRET SANTA
GIFT FOR THESE PEOPLE, MIKE.

1105
00:51:21,580 --> 00:51:23,548
THE BOOK HOW TO HIDE
A MURDER WEAPON.

1106
00:51:23,582 --> 00:51:26,752
OKAY.

1107
00:51:26,785 --> 00:51:29,053
[SERVO SNIFFLES]

1108
00:51:29,087 --> 00:51:30,522
- [SERVO SNEEZES]
- OH, NOT AGAIN.

1109
00:51:30,555 --> 00:51:32,757
LOOK, HERE'S YOUR ALLEGRA.

1110
00:51:32,790 --> 00:51:34,392
OH, THANK-- THANKS.

1111
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:35,693
- THERE YOU GO.
- OH, THAT WAS FAST.

1112
00:51:35,727 --> 00:51:38,197
MM-HMM.

1113
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:39,798
THANKS.

1114
00:51:39,832 --> 00:51:42,300
KILLER GRANDMA GOT BACK.

1115
00:51:47,305 --> 00:51:50,042
I HAVE A FEELING HE'S GONNA
LEAD A LONG, FULL LIFE.

1116
00:51:50,075 --> 00:51:53,945
- YEAH.
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]

1117
00:51:53,978 --> 00:51:56,113
UH, NOW I GOTTA GO OVER
AND BUST GRANDPA WALTON

1118
00:51:56,147 --> 00:51:59,117
FOR RAISING POT.

1119
00:51:59,150 --> 00:52:01,887
OOH, TAKE THREE MEN TO PEEL HIM
OFF THAT SEAT IN HOT WEATHER.

1120
00:52:04,622 --> 00:52:06,625
UNIT ONE,
THIS IS UNIT FOUR, OVER.

1121
00:52:06,658 --> 00:52:08,227
I'LL HANG UP AND LISTEN.

1122
00:52:11,663 --> 00:52:15,133
UNIT ONE,
THIS IS UNIT FOUR, OVER.

1123
00:52:15,167 --> 00:52:19,137
UNIT ONE'S LOOKING
AT THE RADIO, GIGGLING.

1124
00:52:19,170 --> 00:52:20,538
UNIT ONE, OVER.
UNIT THREE, DO YOU READ?

1125
00:52:20,572 --> 00:52:23,175
DO YOU READ?

1126
00:52:23,208 --> 00:52:25,277
[DOLL] MAMA.

1127
00:52:25,310 --> 00:52:26,878
OKAY, HOLD STILL.

1128
00:52:29,747 --> 00:52:31,983
HEY, WHERE'S MY BIKE?
I REPORTED IT STOLEN

1129
00:52:32,017 --> 00:52:34,385
80 YEARS AGO!

1130
00:52:34,418 --> 00:52:36,353
- JEEZ.
- OH.

1131
00:52:38,423 --> 00:52:40,158
WHAT? WHAT?

1132
00:52:42,393 --> 00:52:45,397
WELL, RIGHT ABOUT THEN,
THEM DUKE BOYS SHOWED UP.

1133
00:52:47,598 --> 00:52:50,402
LUCINDA!
LUCINDA!

1134
00:52:50,435 --> 00:52:51,970
GUESS WHO WE SAW IN TOWN?

1135
00:52:52,003 --> 00:52:53,638
BE CALM.

1136
00:52:53,672 --> 00:52:56,173
BE CALM.

1137
00:52:56,207 --> 00:52:58,610
I SUPPOSE YOU'RE GONNA
BLAME ME FOR THIS.

1138
00:53:03,382 --> 00:53:05,383
HERE'S HIS HEAD,
YOU'VE EARNED IT.

1139
00:53:08,487 --> 00:53:10,088
I MEANT TO ASK HIM
IN FOR PIE.

1140
00:53:10,122 --> 00:53:12,323
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED.

1141
00:53:14,292 --> 00:53:17,195
WELL, YOU READY
TO TRY THAT CIDER?

1142
00:53:17,228 --> 00:53:18,563
HELLO?

1143
00:53:18,597 --> 00:53:20,632
MELISSA.

1144
00:53:24,435 --> 00:53:26,103
- OOF.
- UGH.

1145
00:53:26,137 --> 00:53:27,472
[JODIE RETCHES]

1146
00:53:27,505 --> 00:53:30,775
WHOA, HOT DOG, FRENCH FRIES,
RAMEN NOODLES.

1147
00:53:30,808 --> 00:53:33,812
WOW, LOOK AT HIM GO.

1148
00:53:33,845 --> 00:53:36,582
MELISSA.

1149
00:53:36,615 --> 00:53:38,583
GO INSIDE WITH MOLLY.

1150
00:53:38,617 --> 00:53:40,485
- GO AHEAD, GO ON.
- [LUCINDA MUTTERS]

1151
00:53:44,990 --> 00:53:46,825
THIS IS SO WEIRD, YOU KNOW,
THIS HAPPENED TO ME

1152
00:53:46,858 --> 00:53:48,460
ON ONE OF MY FIRST DATES.
GRANDMA KILLED A GUY.

1153
00:53:48,493 --> 00:53:50,395
[BOTS] WHOA.

1154
00:53:50,428 --> 00:53:51,597
DATED THE GIRL
FOR A WHILE, THOUGH.

1155
00:53:51,630 --> 00:53:53,532
- [BOTS] OH.
- YEAH.

1156
00:53:56,167 --> 00:53:57,568
[JODIE RETCHES]

1157
00:53:57,602 --> 00:53:59,938
UM, JODIE, THAT'S GONNA TAKE
THE PAINT OFF YOUR CAR.

1158
00:54:05,143 --> 00:54:06,443
YEAH, YEAH.

1159
00:54:06,477 --> 00:54:07,778
YOU KNOW,
A VOMIT STAIN MAVERICK

1160
00:54:07,812 --> 00:54:09,948
WAS HARDLY A RARITY
IN THOSE DAYS.

1161
00:54:09,982 --> 00:54:12,350
MM, I'M HERE TO TELL YOU,
YOU KNOW?

1162
00:54:12,383 --> 00:54:14,285
[ROOSTER CROWS]

1163
00:54:14,318 --> 00:54:15,687
DID SHE JUST CROW?

1164
00:54:18,423 --> 00:54:20,425
GROSS, SHE'S KNEELING
IN DEPUTY.

1165
00:54:23,762 --> 00:54:26,130
HMM. KILLER GRANDMA.
I'M LOCKED IN A BARN.

1166
00:54:26,163 --> 00:54:29,968
SOMETHING'S NOT RIGHT HERE.

1167
00:54:30,002 --> 00:54:31,637
WHY IS THAT PIGEON
STARING AT MY HEAD?

1168
00:54:31,670 --> 00:54:33,672
[SERVO COOS]

1169
00:54:39,577 --> 00:54:41,713
WELL, AT LEAST THEY DIDN'T CHAIN
HIM TO A BALDWIN BROTHER.

1170
00:54:41,747 --> 00:54:42,880
HE'S GOT THAT GOING FOR HIM.

1171
00:54:42,913 --> 00:54:44,415
WOW.

1172
00:54:49,120 --> 00:54:51,957
HEY, THERE GOES
DON "THE SNAKE" PRUDHOMME.

1173
00:54:56,093 --> 00:54:58,228
WELL, THE CALIFORNIA
BED AND BREAKFAST GUIDE

1174
00:54:58,262 --> 00:55:02,333
IS GETTING AN ANGRY LETTER.

1175
00:55:02,367 --> 00:55:04,202
--JUST DRIVE CAREFULLY.
WE DON'T WANNA BE STOPPED.

1176
00:55:04,235 --> 00:55:07,038
LEFT THE P.A. ON.

1177
00:55:07,072 --> 00:55:08,205
YOU KNOW, FROM THE BACK
SHE LOOKS

1178
00:55:08,238 --> 00:55:09,940
EXACTLY LIKE DAVID CASSIDY.

1179
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:13,110
...NOW HURRY UP AND FOLLOW ME
AND BE CAREFUL.

1180
00:55:13,143 --> 00:55:15,413
- HELLO?
- HELLO?

1181
00:55:19,617 --> 00:55:21,218
WHY DON'T YOU JUST CALL
HARVEY KEITEL OVER

1182
00:55:21,252 --> 00:55:24,222
TO FIX THINGS?

1183
00:55:24,255 --> 00:55:26,223
WHY DO YOU THINK I TURNED
DOWN YOUR ROAD TODAY?

1184
00:55:26,257 --> 00:55:27,892
WHY DID YOU?

1185
00:55:27,925 --> 00:55:30,462
BECAUSE I WANTED TO SEE
WHAT WAS AT THE OTHER END.

1186
00:55:30,495 --> 00:55:32,430
AND I GOT LUCKY BECAUSE
YOU WERE THERE.

1187
00:55:32,463 --> 00:55:34,265
HUH, I HAVE A WEIRD VOICE.

1188
00:55:34,298 --> 00:55:37,135
THEY SAY IN THIS TOWN
THAT I'M A WITCH.

1189
00:55:37,168 --> 00:55:39,603
THEY WON'T FIND HIM
UNTIL HE KILLS AGAIN.

1190
00:55:39,637 --> 00:55:41,840
SHE DOESN'T GO OUT MUCH
BECAUSE OF HER FACE.

1191
00:55:41,873 --> 00:55:43,608
UH, ME, COULD YOU
FAST-FORWARD?

1192
00:55:43,642 --> 00:55:46,177
CAN YOU STAY WITH ME
A FEW DAYS?

1193
00:55:46,210 --> 00:55:48,078
STAY HERE WITH ME?

1194
00:55:48,112 --> 00:55:49,680
I'M LONELY, JODIE.

1195
00:55:49,713 --> 00:55:51,648
[FADING] I'M LONELY, JODIE.

1196
00:55:51,682 --> 00:55:53,785
I NEED SOMEONE TO TALK TO.

1197
00:55:53,818 --> 00:55:56,020
[FADING] I NEED
SOMEONE TO TALK TO.

1198
00:55:56,053 --> 00:55:59,123
TO SHARE THINGS WITH,
JUST FOR A FEW DAYS.

1199
00:55:59,157 --> 00:56:01,092
OH, YEP, THERE--
THERE'S WHERE I TRIPPED UP.

1200
00:56:01,125 --> 00:56:03,695
YEP.

1201
00:56:03,728 --> 00:56:05,863
UM, I'VE BEEN APPOINTED
AS YOUR DEFENSE.

1202
00:56:08,867 --> 00:56:10,535
SO YOU DONE
BLOWING GROCERIES?

1203
00:56:13,337 --> 00:56:15,140
NOT GONNA "ZAH" YOUR WAY
OUT OF THIS ONE,

1204
00:56:15,173 --> 00:56:17,975
ARE YOU, PALLIE?

1205
00:56:18,008 --> 00:56:21,145
WHAT'RE THEY GOING
TO DO ABOUT ME?

1206
00:56:21,178 --> 00:56:23,548
I DON'T KNOW.

1207
00:56:23,582 --> 00:56:24,748
I'M GONNA TIME THIS PAUSE.

1208
00:56:24,782 --> 00:56:26,985
ONE, TWO, THREE, FOUR,

1209
00:56:27,018 --> 00:56:29,153
FIVE-- WOW.
FIVE SIX SEVEN--

1210
00:56:29,187 --> 00:56:31,655
WILL YOU STAY HERE
UNTIL TOMORROW?

1211
00:56:31,688 --> 00:56:33,992
WELL, I DO WANNA TRY
GRANDMA'S WAFFLES.

1212
00:56:34,025 --> 00:56:37,095
I DON'T SEEM
TO HAVE ANY CHOICE.

1213
00:56:37,128 --> 00:56:40,898
LUTHER'LL UNLOCK THAT
AS SOON AS HE GETS BACK.

1214
00:56:40,932 --> 00:56:42,533
THEY'RE JUST PAUSING
OUT OF SPITE, NOW.

1215
00:56:42,567 --> 00:56:45,437
- YEAH.
- TRUST ME
NOT TO RUN OFF?

1216
00:56:45,470 --> 00:56:46,905
HE'LL DO WHAT I SAY.

1217
00:56:46,938 --> 00:56:50,108
I'VE GOT PICTURES
OF HIM WITH MOM.

1218
00:56:50,142 --> 00:56:53,210
BELIEVE ME.

1219
00:56:53,243 --> 00:56:54,678
LISTEN, THAT OLD WOMAN--

1220
00:56:54,712 --> 00:56:57,448
JUST GIVE US UNTIL TOMORROW.

1221
00:56:57,482 --> 00:56:58,583
PLEASE?

1222
00:56:58,617 --> 00:56:59,950
AND WHAT GOOD WILL THAT DO?

1223
00:56:59,983 --> 00:57:02,853
IT WON'T CHANGE ANYTHING.

1224
00:57:02,887 --> 00:57:06,257
MAYBE I CAN FIND A WAY
FOR YOU TO UNDERSTAND.

1225
00:57:06,290 --> 00:57:08,527
OH, I UNDERSTAND.

1226
00:57:08,560 --> 00:57:10,060
I UNDERSTAND ENOUGH
TO KNOW THAT

1227
00:57:10,093 --> 00:57:11,562
IF YOU'D GONE TO THAT
SHERIFF TEN DAYS AGO,

1228
00:57:11,595 --> 00:57:13,030
THAT DEPUTY WOULD
STILL BE ALIVE.

1229
00:57:13,063 --> 00:57:16,367
AH, LOOK, WE DON'T
KNOW HE'S DEAD.

1230
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:19,237
SHE KILLED THAT FARMER
TOO, DIDN'T SHE?

1231
00:57:19,270 --> 00:57:21,138
DIDN'T SHE?

1232
00:57:21,172 --> 00:57:22,373
DID ALL THE ACTORS DRINK

1233
00:57:22,407 --> 00:57:25,075
A QUART OF ROBITUSSIN
BEFORE SHOOTING?

1234
00:57:25,108 --> 00:57:26,743
IT'S WRONG, MELISSA.

1235
00:57:26,777 --> 00:57:30,348
LUTHER AND MOLLY
AND YOU ARE WRONG.

1236
00:57:30,382 --> 00:57:32,750
- WE'RE CURSED.
- NO.

1237
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:34,352
WE ARE CURSED.

1238
00:57:34,385 --> 00:57:36,253
COME ON, WE'RE CURSED,
PLEASE?

1239
00:57:36,287 --> 00:57:37,688
YOU BELIEVE THAT.

1240
00:57:37,722 --> 00:57:41,592
YOU REALLY DO BELIEVE IT.

1241
00:57:41,625 --> 00:57:44,262
YES.

1242
00:57:44,295 --> 00:57:45,463
IF I STAY UNTIL TOMORROW,

1243
00:57:45,497 --> 00:57:48,465
WILL YOU GO AWAY WITH ME?

1244
00:57:48,500 --> 00:57:49,833
WHERE?

1245
00:57:49,867 --> 00:57:51,502
TO THE SHERIFF,
AND THEN, AFTER THAT,

1246
00:57:51,535 --> 00:57:53,203
AWAY FROM HERE.

1247
00:57:53,237 --> 00:57:55,707
MAYBE BACK TO AUSTIN
WITH ME.

1248
00:57:55,740 --> 00:57:57,475
I CAN NEVER LEAVE THEM.

1249
00:57:57,508 --> 00:57:59,443
ANYWAY, I HATE LINE-DANCING.

1250
00:57:59,477 --> 00:58:02,180
WHY? WHY, MELISSA?

1251
00:58:02,213 --> 00:58:05,015
WHAT HAPPENS TO MY FAMILY
IS MY RESPONSIBILITY?

1252
00:58:05,048 --> 00:58:07,018
AND WHY NOT LUTHER?
IT'S HIS FAMILY.

1253
00:58:07,052 --> 00:58:08,820
YOU SAW LUCINDA
THIS AFTERNOON.

1254
00:58:08,853 --> 00:58:10,388
SHE BARELY KNOWS
MOLLY OR LUTHER

1255
00:58:10,422 --> 00:58:13,525
OR ANYONE EXISTS BUT ME.

1256
00:58:13,558 --> 00:58:15,025
I SAVED HER.

1257
00:58:15,058 --> 00:58:17,528
I'M THE ONLY ONE
THAT CAN REACH HER.

1258
00:58:17,562 --> 00:58:18,697
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1259
00:58:18,730 --> 00:58:20,732
MUCH OF... ANYTHING, REALLY.

1260
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:25,002
THEN STAY.

1261
00:58:25,035 --> 00:58:27,238
JUST ONE MORE DAY.

1262
00:58:27,272 --> 00:58:29,873
OH, YOU MEAN "STAAAAAY!"

1263
00:58:29,907 --> 00:58:31,408
ALL RIGHT.

1264
00:58:31,442 --> 00:58:35,347
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN, THE MOST
MALLEABLE MAN IN THE WORLD.

1265
00:58:35,380 --> 00:58:36,847
I'LL FIND A WAY.

1266
00:58:36,882 --> 00:58:39,950
COME ON, WE'LL HAVE
A NICE MURDER-FREE WALK.

1267
00:58:39,983 --> 00:58:41,852
YOU REALLY DO BELIEVE
THERE'S SOME--

1268
00:58:41,887 --> 00:58:43,788
BOLOGNA LEFT.

1269
00:58:43,822 --> 00:58:46,790
SOME DEVIL OUT THERE.

1270
00:58:46,823 --> 00:58:48,125
OH YES.

1271
00:58:48,158 --> 00:58:50,127
I'VE SEEN HIS FOOD CAKE.

1272
00:58:50,160 --> 00:58:52,130
I SUPPOSE THAT
MAKES IT TRUE.

1273
00:58:52,163 --> 00:58:54,098
- [SERVO SIGHS]
- IT IS TRUE.

1274
00:58:54,132 --> 00:58:57,268
TALK! QUICKER!

1275
00:58:57,302 --> 00:59:01,238
JUST LIKE THOSE PEOPLE
IN THE STORE.

1276
00:59:01,272 --> 00:59:04,875
THEY BELIEVE YOU'RE A WITCH,
SO IT'S TRUE FOR THEM.

1277
00:59:04,908 --> 00:59:07,645
WELL, I DON'T,
SO YOU'RE NOT.

1278
00:59:07,678 --> 00:59:09,980
I'M POSSESSED BY THE DEVIL.

1279
00:59:10,013 --> 00:59:11,482
MICHAEL EISNER?

1280
00:59:11,515 --> 00:59:13,618
THERE'S NO SUCH THING.

1281
00:59:13,652 --> 00:59:15,287
I LEARNED THAT
IN COMMUNITY COLLEGE.

1282
00:59:15,320 --> 00:59:16,720
I HEARD HIS VOICE.

1283
00:59:16,753 --> 00:59:20,325
HE SANG "LEND ME A TENOR."

1284
00:59:20,358 --> 00:59:22,427
NO.

1285
00:59:22,460 --> 00:59:24,628
THERE IS NO DEVIL.

1286
00:59:26,932 --> 00:59:29,767
HUH.

1287
00:59:29,800 --> 00:59:31,568
BROUGHT TO YOU BY
THE NATIONAL COUNCIL

1288
00:59:31,602 --> 00:59:33,705
FOR EMERGENCY BRAKES.

1289
00:59:37,842 --> 00:59:39,610
I THINK THERE USED
TO BE A LAKE HERE.

1290
00:59:39,643 --> 00:59:41,078
DAMN.

1291
00:59:44,048 --> 00:59:46,117
LESSON: NEVER ASK
KELSEY GRAMMER

1292
00:59:46,150 --> 00:59:47,685
TO GET YOUR GLOVES
OUT OF YOUR CAR.

1293
00:59:52,390 --> 00:59:54,558
NOW HE'S HANDCUFFED
TO THE MEATLOAF.

1294
00:59:58,028 --> 01:00:00,063
I JUST SAID THE STEAK
WAS A LITTLE TOUGH.

1295
01:00:00,097 --> 01:00:01,598
I DIDN'T MEAN TO BRING
EVERYONE DOWN.

1296
01:00:04,735 --> 01:00:07,672
AH, SO YOU'RE
JUDGING US NOW.

1297
01:00:10,675 --> 01:00:12,777
YOU TOOK TOO MANY
PORK CHOPS.

1298
01:00:20,352 --> 01:00:22,020
I SAW A ROBIN TODAY.

1299
01:00:25,188 --> 01:00:28,358
I COULD PUT MY SALAD FORK
RIGHT IN HIS JUGULAR.

1300
01:00:31,028 --> 01:00:32,697
WELL, I'M JUST GONNA
STAY THROUGH THE WEEK,

1301
01:00:32,730 --> 01:00:35,900
AND THAT'S IT.

1302
01:00:35,933 --> 01:00:37,335
I'LL GO LOCK MYSELF
IN THE BARN.

1303
01:00:37,368 --> 01:00:40,572
DON'T GET UP.

1304
01:00:40,605 --> 01:00:43,240
HONEY, I FOUND THE DEPUTY'S
BADGE IN MY STEW.

1305
01:00:43,273 --> 01:00:44,875
OH.

1306
01:00:54,118 --> 01:00:56,920
HMM, NEED THAT SCOTTISH GUY
TO COME OVER

1307
01:00:56,953 --> 01:00:58,690
AND SEAL UP MY WINDOWS.

1308
01:01:01,358 --> 01:01:03,227
MUST BE HARD GETTING
WHALE OIL ANYMORE

1309
01:01:03,260 --> 01:01:05,730
FOR THESE LAMPS.

1310
01:01:05,763 --> 01:01:07,698
CHECK IT OUT, SHE'S DRESSED
LIKE ED AMES.

1311
01:01:10,435 --> 01:01:13,603
♪ SKIP-A-ROPE ♪

1312
01:01:13,637 --> 01:01:15,707
DEAD RUBBER CHICKEN?
WHAT IS THAT?

1313
01:01:20,043 --> 01:01:22,547
TIME TO GO BE A GENERAL
IN THE MICHIGAN MILITIA.

1314
01:01:25,182 --> 01:01:27,718
OH, I MADE A TERRIBLE
SOCK MONKEY.

1315
01:01:34,158 --> 01:01:36,127
MY OBSESSION WITH
THE COLOR BROWN

1316
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:37,728
IS GETTING OUT OF HAND.

1317
01:01:43,233 --> 01:01:45,703
SOMEONE'S PLAYING THE CICADA
IN THE BACKGROUND.

1318
01:01:48,072 --> 01:01:50,207
[ALL] OH! HEY!

1319
01:01:50,240 --> 01:01:53,677
[ALL] AAH!

1320
01:01:53,710 --> 01:01:55,747
THE EDITOR GOT CALLED OUT
OF THE ROOM A LOT, I GUESS.

1321
01:01:58,182 --> 01:01:59,417
CAN'T STOP THINKING ABOUT

1322
01:01:59,450 --> 01:02:01,018
THAT SANDWICH I HAD
THE OTHER DAY.

1323
01:02:03,922 --> 01:02:06,390
[SERVO HUMS ALONG]

1324
01:02:08,458 --> 01:02:10,260
IT'S THE LONELIEST FIREFLY.

1325
01:02:10,293 --> 01:02:11,928
AND HIS FRIENDS.

1326
01:02:15,065 --> 01:02:17,335
HARPSICHORD IS REALLY
A STUPID INSTRUMENT.

1327
01:02:17,368 --> 01:02:19,170
- WOW.
- I'M SORRY,
I'M IN A BAD MOOD.

1328
01:02:19,203 --> 01:02:22,540
OH, UNDERSTOOD.

1329
01:02:22,573 --> 01:02:24,575
BINDING POLYMERS AND YOU!

1330
01:02:27,212 --> 01:02:29,447
[PEOPLE CHANT]
BURN THE WITCH!
BURN THE WITCH!

1331
01:02:29,480 --> 01:02:32,550
[CHANT CONTINUES]

1332
01:02:32,583 --> 01:02:34,618
OH, AND GO PACKERS TOO.

1333
01:02:34,652 --> 01:02:36,920
BUT MOSTLY, BURN THE WITCH.

1334
01:02:36,953 --> 01:02:39,690
"THE WICKED MAN

1335
01:02:39,723 --> 01:02:42,360
"TRAVAILETH WITH PAIN

1336
01:02:42,393 --> 01:02:43,460
ALL HIS DAYS."

1337
01:02:43,493 --> 01:02:44,928
...SAID MADELEINE.

1338
01:02:44,962 --> 01:02:47,898
"AND THE NUMBER OF YEARS

1339
01:02:47,932 --> 01:02:50,868
IS HIDDEN TO THE OPPRESSOR."

1340
01:02:50,902 --> 01:02:52,603
BUNCH OF CRAP.

1341
01:02:52,637 --> 01:02:54,738
"A DREADFUL SONG
IS IN HIS EARS."

1342
01:02:54,772 --> 01:02:56,307
IT'S PAULA COLE, I THINK.

1343
01:02:56,340 --> 01:02:58,342
"IN PROSPERITY,

1344
01:02:58,375 --> 01:03:00,277
"THE DESTROYER

1345
01:03:00,310 --> 01:03:02,813
SHALL COME UPON HIM."

1346
01:03:02,847 --> 01:03:04,015
WHAT IS IT, CHILD?

1347
01:03:04,048 --> 01:03:06,017
I HEARD SOMETHING.

1348
01:03:06,050 --> 01:03:07,485
PAY ATTENTION

1349
01:03:07,518 --> 01:03:09,187
TO THE WORD OF GOD.

1350
01:03:09,220 --> 01:03:12,690
FOR HE LOVES YOU, AND HE MAY
KILL YOU IF YOU DON'T.

1351
01:03:12,723 --> 01:03:15,125
- YEA--
- TEAM.

1352
01:03:15,158 --> 01:03:17,928
"THE LIGHT OF THE WICKED

1353
01:03:17,962 --> 01:03:20,532
- SHALL BE PUT OUT--"
- BY 10:30.

1354
01:03:20,565 --> 01:03:23,868
"AND THE SPARK OF HIS FIRE

1355
01:03:23,902 --> 01:03:25,268
SHALL NOT SHINE."

1356
01:03:25,302 --> 01:03:27,172
JUST TAKE THE OLD-FASHIONED
PHOTO, DAD.

1357
01:03:27,205 --> 01:03:29,507
"THE LIGHT SHALL BE DARK

1358
01:03:29,540 --> 01:03:31,475
"IN HIS TABERNACLE.

1359
01:03:31,508 --> 01:03:33,643
"AND HIS CANDLE

1360
01:03:33,677 --> 01:03:36,180
SHALL BE PUT OUT WITH HIM."

1361
01:03:36,213 --> 01:03:37,715
LISTEN.

1362
01:03:37,748 --> 01:03:39,117
SIT BACK, LUCINDA.

1363
01:03:39,150 --> 01:03:41,685
IT'S ANN ELLER.

1364
01:03:41,718 --> 01:03:43,187
THEY'RE COMING FOR ME.

1365
01:03:43,220 --> 01:03:45,890
CALM YOURSELF, SIT BACK.

1366
01:03:48,258 --> 01:03:50,628
SO THIS FAMILY HAS BEEN
PAUSING FOR CENTURIES.

1367
01:03:50,662 --> 01:03:51,695
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]
- IT'S A TRADITION.

1368
01:03:51,728 --> 01:03:54,998
"THE STEPS OF HIS STRENGTH

1369
01:03:55,032 --> 01:03:56,467
SHALL BE STRAIGHTENED--"

1370
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:58,368
UH, THIS DOES DRAG,
DOESN'T IT?

1371
01:03:58,402 --> 01:04:01,338
"AND HIS OWN COUNSEL

1372
01:04:02,973 --> 01:04:06,743
"CAST HIM DOWN.

1373
01:04:06,777 --> 01:04:10,582
- FOR HE IS CAST..."
- OUT OF PLASTIC.

1374
01:04:10,615 --> 01:04:12,417
[DISTANT CHANTING]
BURN THE WITCH!

1375
01:04:12,450 --> 01:04:16,287
YE-- YES?

1376
01:04:16,320 --> 01:04:19,623
"FOR HE IS CAST

1377
01:04:19,657 --> 01:04:21,858
INTO A NET..."

1378
01:04:21,892 --> 01:04:23,293
AND IT JUST
GOES ON FROM THERE.

1379
01:04:26,130 --> 01:04:28,732
OH-- OH, THAT'S RIGHT,
I CALLED A SERVICE

1380
01:04:28,765 --> 01:04:29,900
TO COME AROUND
AND BURN MY WITCH.

1381
01:04:29,933 --> 01:04:31,768
WHAT IS IT, DAVID?

1382
01:04:31,802 --> 01:04:32,937
IT'S PEOPLE SAYING,
"BURN THE WITCH."

1383
01:04:32,970 --> 01:04:34,038
YOU DEAF?

1384
01:04:34,072 --> 01:04:36,607
BURN THE WITCH!
BURN THE WITCH!

1385
01:04:38,475 --> 01:04:40,612
PAPA, WHAT IS IT?

1386
01:04:40,645 --> 01:04:42,112
PEOPLE SAYING
"BURN THE WITCH"!

1387
01:04:42,145 --> 01:04:44,315
DO YOU HAVE ANY
DEDUCTIVE POWERS AT ALL?

1388
01:04:44,348 --> 01:04:46,317
I DON'T KNOW YET.

1389
01:04:46,350 --> 01:04:48,818
TAKE YOU MOTHER TO
THE BACK OF THE HOUSE.

1390
01:04:48,852 --> 01:04:50,220
WORK HER OVER.

1391
01:04:50,253 --> 01:04:52,490
AND I'LL SEE WHAT
THIS IS ABOUT.

1392
01:04:52,523 --> 01:04:54,292
BURN THE WITCH...

1393
01:04:54,325 --> 01:04:55,727
IT'S PRETTY CASUAL,
IT'S KIND OF LIKE

1394
01:04:55,760 --> 01:04:59,230
A LAKE WOBEGONE
WITCH BURNING.

1395
01:04:59,263 --> 01:05:01,165
[SERVO AS GARRISON KEILLOR]
BURNING THE WITCH.

1396
01:05:01,198 --> 01:05:02,333
IS THAT YOU GUYS
BURNIN' WITCHES?

1397
01:05:02,367 --> 01:05:05,937
CAN I COME?

1398
01:05:05,970 --> 01:05:09,340
HEY, HOSS HAS
LOST SOME WEIGHT.

1399
01:05:09,373 --> 01:05:10,975
UH...

1400
01:05:11,008 --> 01:05:13,610
WE WAS OUT BURNIN', UM,
THE-- UM--

1401
01:05:13,643 --> 01:05:17,448
YOU TELL HIM.

1402
01:05:17,482 --> 01:05:20,217
UM, SEEM KIND OF SILLY NOW.

1403
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:23,320
GOOD EVENING, MR. KEITEL.

1404
01:05:23,353 --> 01:05:24,855
MR. STRICKLAND.

1405
01:05:24,888 --> 01:05:27,157
YOU'VE BEEN HITTIN'
THE BOOZE AGAIN!

1406
01:05:27,190 --> 01:05:28,725
WHAT CAN I DO FOR YOU?

1407
01:05:28,758 --> 01:05:30,662
UM.

1408
01:05:30,695 --> 01:05:34,165
MRS. LUCASTA LOST
HER YOUNG'UN TONIGHT.

1409
01:05:34,198 --> 01:05:35,465
ONLY THREE YEARS OLD.

1410
01:05:35,498 --> 01:05:37,368
LEFT HER AT GYMBOREE.

1411
01:05:37,402 --> 01:05:40,370
I'M SORRY TO HEAR THAT.

1412
01:05:40,403 --> 01:05:41,838
KESTER HAGEN HERE

1413
01:05:41,872 --> 01:05:43,540
LOST THREE HEAD
OF COW TONIGHT,

1414
01:05:43,573 --> 01:05:46,243
AND HIS WIFE IS DOWN SICK.

1415
01:05:46,277 --> 01:05:47,378
I'M SORRY.

1416
01:05:47,412 --> 01:05:49,180
AND MY SOUFFLE FELL TODAY.

1417
01:05:49,213 --> 01:05:51,348
--PLAGUE.

1418
01:05:51,382 --> 01:05:53,583
- I UNDERSTAND.
- PLAGUE.

1419
01:05:53,617 --> 01:05:55,418
THE PLAGUE HAS HIT

1420
01:05:55,452 --> 01:05:57,722
NEAR EVERYBODY HERE,
DAVID STRICKLAND.

1421
01:05:57,755 --> 01:06:00,658
BUT IT AIN'T HIT YOU.
NOW HOW DO YOU EXPLAIN THAT?

1422
01:06:00,692 --> 01:06:02,727
WELL, I DON'T COMB MY HAIR
WITH RAT BONES.

1423
01:06:02,760 --> 01:06:06,397
WELL, I CAN ONLY ASSUME--

1424
01:06:06,430 --> 01:06:08,832
THAT I'M FRANZ SCHUBERT.

1425
01:06:08,865 --> 01:06:11,735
THAT IT'S GOD'S WILL.

1426
01:06:11,768 --> 01:06:14,872
DON'T TALK TO US ABOUT GOD,
DAVID STRICKLAND.

1427
01:06:14,905 --> 01:06:16,207
THERE'S A WITCH
IN THAT HOUSE.

1428
01:06:16,240 --> 01:06:18,142
AND WE AIM TO HAVE HER.

1429
01:06:18,175 --> 01:06:21,245
THERE IS NO WITCH
IN THAT HOUSE.

1430
01:06:21,278 --> 01:06:22,913
WELL, MY DAUGHTER'S KIND OF
A WITCH, BUT OTHER THAN THAT,

1431
01:06:22,947 --> 01:06:25,817
- NO WITCHES.
- GO ON HOME!

1432
01:06:25,850 --> 01:06:29,053
WE WILL NOT GO HOME UNTIL
WE GET WHAT WE COME FOR.

1433
01:06:29,087 --> 01:06:31,555
YOUR DAUGHTER IS A WITCH,
AND SHE'S PUT A HEX ON US.

1434
01:06:31,588 --> 01:06:34,758
THAT'S A DAMN FOOL
THING TO SAY, MR. KEITEL.

1435
01:06:36,193 --> 01:06:38,295
GO ON HOME.

1436
01:06:38,328 --> 01:06:39,563
HAH, LOOK AT 'EM GO.

1437
01:06:39,597 --> 01:06:42,400
RUN, YOU YELLOW-BELLIED--
OH, YOU'RE NOT.

1438
01:06:42,433 --> 01:06:45,435
I'LL TALK TO YOU TOMORROW
DOWN AT BEN PROCTER'S STORE.

1439
01:06:45,468 --> 01:06:46,970
THERE'LL BE NO TALK.

1440
01:06:47,003 --> 01:06:48,305
WE'LL HAVE THE WITCH.

1441
01:06:48,338 --> 01:06:51,508
OVER MY DEAD BODY!

1442
01:06:51,542 --> 01:06:55,312
- UH-OH.
- SO BE IT.

1443
01:06:55,345 --> 01:06:58,782
- COME ON.
- SMOOTH, STRICKLAND.

1444
01:06:58,815 --> 01:07:00,450
[STRICKLAND SCREAMS]

1445
01:07:00,483 --> 01:07:03,953
TAKE MY DAUGHTER, BUT SPARE
MY COMMEMORATIVE PLATES!

1446
01:07:03,987 --> 01:07:06,857
RUN, LUCINDA!

1447
01:07:26,177 --> 01:07:28,178
[MUMBLES]

1448
01:07:31,348 --> 01:07:32,683
AAH!

1449
01:07:32,717 --> 01:07:34,185
HEY, HEY, WHO ARE YOU?

1450
01:07:34,218 --> 01:07:36,053
SERVO, STOP IT!
WHAT'RE YOU DOING?

1451
01:07:36,087 --> 01:07:38,388
- SERVO, HEAVEN'S SAKE!
- [SERVO HUMS]

1452
01:07:38,422 --> 01:07:39,990
HI, MIKE, WHAT-- GRANDMA!

1453
01:07:40,023 --> 01:07:41,558
DARN IT, GRANDMA, STOP.

1454
01:07:41,592 --> 01:07:42,827
NOW, I TOLD YOU NO.

1455
01:07:42,860 --> 01:07:44,762
JEEZ, I'M SORRY, MIKE.

1456
01:07:44,795 --> 01:07:46,830
WAIT A MINUTE,
THIS IS YOUR GRANDMA?

1457
01:07:46,863 --> 01:07:48,698
SURE IS, MIKE.
ISN'T SHE SPRY?

1458
01:07:48,732 --> 01:07:50,533
WHEN DID YOU GET A GRANDMA?

1459
01:07:50,567 --> 01:07:53,070
I HAVE TWO GRANDMAS,
MIKE, I ALWAYS HAVE.

1460
01:07:53,103 --> 01:07:55,005
THE OTHER ONE DOESN'T
KILL PEOPLE, THOUGH.
THIS ONE DOES.

1461
01:07:55,038 --> 01:07:56,207
THAT'S HOW
I TELL THEM APART.

1462
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:57,842
NOW, GRANDMA, DOWN.
DOWN, GRANDMA.

1463
01:07:57,875 --> 01:07:59,377
UH, I GUESS IT'S OKAY.

1464
01:07:59,410 --> 01:08:01,245
I MEAN, COULDN'T YOU
GET HER A TV OR SOMETHING?

1465
01:08:01,278 --> 01:08:02,947
HOLD ON A SECOND.
WHAT-- WHAT'S THAT, GRANDMA?

1466
01:08:02,980 --> 01:08:05,048
BIG... SLOW,
TEMPTING TARGET.

1467
01:08:05,082 --> 01:08:06,517
OH, BELIEVE ME, I KNOW.

1468
01:08:06,550 --> 01:08:08,585
BUT YOU JUST CAN'T, OKAY?

1469
01:08:08,618 --> 01:08:09,953
WELL, I TELL YOU WHAT, MIKE.

1470
01:08:09,987 --> 01:08:11,222
I'M JUST GONNA
LEAVE YOU TWO ALONE

1471
01:08:11,255 --> 01:08:13,057
TO START ALL OVER WITH
EACH OTHER, ALL RIGHT?

1472
01:08:13,090 --> 01:08:15,058
- NO, SERVO, DON'T.
- AH, SHE'S FULL
OF STORIES, MIKE.

1473
01:08:15,092 --> 01:08:16,593
HAVE A GOOD TIME.

1474
01:08:16,627 --> 01:08:18,262
HEY, HEY, GET AWAY FROM ME.

1475
01:08:18,295 --> 01:08:19,597
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1476
01:08:19,630 --> 01:08:21,632
BACK OFF, LADY-- WHAT?

1477
01:08:21,665 --> 01:08:23,967
WHAT? I'M SORRY,
I DIDN'T CATCH THAT.

1478
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:26,037
- [GRANNY SERVO SCREAMS]
- OW! HEY, LADY!

1479
01:08:26,070 --> 01:08:28,505
STOP IT! STOP! NOW!
BACK DOWN! DOWN! DOWN!

1480
01:08:36,280 --> 01:08:38,115
NO, YOU'RE HURTING ME!

1481
01:08:38,148 --> 01:08:39,783
AHH.

1482
01:08:39,817 --> 01:08:41,485
DON'T THESE PEOPLE
HAVE BUTTER TO CHURN?

1483
01:08:41,518 --> 01:08:43,920
TAFFY TO PULL?
PRAIRIE LAKES TO FORM?

1484
01:08:43,953 --> 01:08:46,457
SOMETHING.

1485
01:08:46,490 --> 01:08:49,427
PLEASE DON'T
TIE ME UP THERE!

1486
01:08:49,460 --> 01:08:50,527
QUIT WHINING.

1487
01:08:50,560 --> 01:08:52,830
OH! NO!

1488
01:08:52,863 --> 01:08:55,265
NO! NO!

1489
01:08:55,298 --> 01:08:56,800
HELP ME!
LET ME DOWN FROM HERE.

1490
01:08:56,833 --> 01:08:58,168
HEY, NEIL YOUNG.

1491
01:08:58,202 --> 01:09:00,270
OH NO, YOU'RE
MAKING A MISTAKE.

1492
01:09:00,303 --> 01:09:02,840
HELP ME.
HELP ME, MELISSA.

1493
01:09:02,873 --> 01:09:05,877
HEY, YOU'VE BEEN
WORKING OUT?

1494
01:09:05,910 --> 01:09:07,845
YOU KNOW, MAYBE
IF THE AMISH USED BUTTONS

1495
01:09:07,878 --> 01:09:10,213
THEY WOULDN'T
BE SO IRRATIONAL.

1496
01:09:10,247 --> 01:09:12,115
NO! NO!

1497
01:09:12,148 --> 01:09:14,117
- PLEASE, YOU'RE HURTING ME!
- NO!

1498
01:09:14,150 --> 01:09:16,653
- BURN THE WITCH.
- YEAH, THAT'S THE PLAN, AMOS.

1499
01:09:16,687 --> 01:09:18,222
- NO!
- KILL THE WITCH.

1500
01:09:18,255 --> 01:09:22,125
- KILL THE WITCH.
KILL THE WITCH.
- [GIRLS SCREAM]

1501
01:09:22,158 --> 01:09:23,827
OH, THIS IS SO GAUCHE.

1502
01:09:23,860 --> 01:09:25,628
MOLLY, PLEASE HELP ME!

1503
01:09:25,662 --> 01:09:27,832
PLEASE DON'T DO THIS!

1504
01:09:27,865 --> 01:09:29,767
[CROWD]
♪ AMAZING ♪

1505
01:09:29,800 --> 01:09:32,368
- TAKE HER DOWN!
- ♪ GRACE ♪

1506
01:09:32,402 --> 01:09:35,605
- HELP, SOMEBODY HELP!
- ♪ HOW SWEET THE SOUND ♪

1507
01:09:35,638 --> 01:09:38,742
- DAMN YOU!
- EVERY WEEK WE DO THIS!

1508
01:09:38,775 --> 01:09:41,212
ANYBODY, I BEG OF YOU!

1509
01:09:41,245 --> 01:09:43,080
ANYBODY, HELP US!

1510
01:09:45,482 --> 01:09:47,183
♪ THIS SONG ♪

1511
01:09:47,217 --> 01:09:49,220
♪ IS IN ♪

1512
01:09:49,253 --> 01:09:52,122
♪ THE PUBLIC ♪

1513
01:09:52,155 --> 01:09:54,023
♪ DOMAIN ♪

1514
01:09:54,057 --> 01:09:56,393
♪ THAT'S WHY ♪

1515
01:09:56,427 --> 01:09:59,463
♪ WE USED IT ♪

1516
01:09:59,497 --> 01:10:02,567
♪ TWICE ♪

1517
01:10:02,600 --> 01:10:05,402
WILL YOU SAVE HER?

1518
01:10:05,435 --> 01:10:08,205
I SAY AGAIN,

1519
01:10:08,238 --> 01:10:09,773
WOULD YOU SAVE THE WITCH?

1520
01:10:09,807 --> 01:10:13,443
SHALL I WRAP HER UP
FOR YOU?

1521
01:10:13,477 --> 01:10:15,947
YES. SAVE HER.

1522
01:10:15,980 --> 01:10:17,380
YOU'VE BEEN
HITTING THE BOOZE?

1523
01:10:17,413 --> 01:10:20,250
WILL YOU ACCEPT ME
AS YOUR MASTER?

1524
01:10:20,283 --> 01:10:21,718
AND GO FETCH?

1525
01:10:21,752 --> 01:10:23,820
YES. YES.

1526
01:10:26,523 --> 01:10:27,658
HOLD UP YOUR HAND.

1527
01:10:27,692 --> 01:10:29,225
LET ME STAMP IT.

1528
01:10:29,260 --> 01:10:31,462
NOW.

1529
01:10:31,495 --> 01:10:32,763
PUT OUT THE FIRE.

1530
01:10:36,200 --> 01:10:37,835
HUH.

1531
01:10:37,868 --> 01:10:41,605
CALEB, WHAT KIND
OF CHARCOAL DID YOU USE?

1532
01:10:41,638 --> 01:10:45,475
MUST'VE GOT A HOLD
OF A WET WITCH.

1533
01:10:45,508 --> 01:10:48,645
YOU HAVE ASKED FOR DEATH.

1534
01:10:48,678 --> 01:10:51,282
AND YOU SHALL HAVE IT.

1535
01:10:51,315 --> 01:10:53,983
MAY YOUR LIVESTOCK
SICKEN AND DIE.

1536
01:10:54,017 --> 01:10:55,285
MOO-- PLUNK.

1537
01:10:55,318 --> 01:10:57,387
MAY YOUR CROPS
ROT ON THE GROUND.

1538
01:10:57,420 --> 01:10:59,122
HAPPENED ALREADY.

1539
01:10:59,155 --> 01:11:02,058
MAY YOUR HOUSES BE INFESTED
WITH SNAKES AND SCORPIONS.

1540
01:11:02,092 --> 01:11:03,860
HOUSES? YOU HAVE HOUSES?

1541
01:11:03,893 --> 01:11:06,363
AND MAY YOUR FIRSTBORN
BE DEFORMED

1542
01:11:06,397 --> 01:11:08,032
AS PIGS AND TOADS!

1543
01:11:08,065 --> 01:11:10,233
MAY YOUR TOMATOES
BE FLAVORLESS!

1544
01:11:10,267 --> 01:11:12,068
[CROWD SCREAMS]

1545
01:11:12,102 --> 01:11:14,170
LET'S BURN SOME
BEATLES RECORDS INSTEAD!

1546
01:11:20,910 --> 01:11:22,512
DID I DO OKAY
WITH THE CURSES?

1547
01:11:22,545 --> 01:11:24,247
I'M OPEN TO CRITICISM.

1548
01:11:29,052 --> 01:11:32,355
[SERVO HUMS ALONG]

1549
01:11:32,388 --> 01:11:34,625
OOH, OUCH, YOU'RE--
YOU'RE STILL HOT, OW.

1550
01:11:39,228 --> 01:11:40,830
YOU KNOW WHAT,
THOSE VILLAGERS

1551
01:11:40,863 --> 01:11:42,667
REALLY BURN ME UP.
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1552
01:11:42,700 --> 01:11:44,402
IT'S GOOD I CAN LAUGH.

1553
01:11:46,937 --> 01:11:48,938
WHO ARE YOU?

1554
01:11:48,972 --> 01:11:51,575
I AM THE FRIEND
AND COMPANION OF THE NIGHT.

1555
01:11:51,608 --> 01:11:53,543
I REJOICE IN SPILLED BLOOD

1556
01:11:53,577 --> 01:11:55,445
- AND THE BAYING OF DOGS.
- [ALL] OH.

1557
01:11:55,478 --> 01:11:58,482
I WANDER AMONG
THE SHADES AND TOMBS.

1558
01:11:58,515 --> 01:12:01,585
I AM GORGO AND MORMO

1559
01:12:01,618 --> 01:12:03,420
OF THE THOUSAND-FACED MOON.

1560
01:12:03,453 --> 01:12:04,788
BUT CALL ME SUE.

1561
01:12:04,822 --> 01:12:07,290
WHAT WOULD YOU HAVE OF ME?

1562
01:12:07,323 --> 01:12:08,958
I ASK...

1563
01:12:08,992 --> 01:12:11,728
THAT YOU KNOW ME
WHEN I RETURN.

1564
01:12:11,762 --> 01:12:14,598
I WILL RETURN.

1565
01:12:14,632 --> 01:12:16,067
[FADING] I WILL RETURN.

1566
01:12:16,100 --> 01:12:18,302
HOLD ON, I'M GETTING A CALL
FROM MARGOT ADLER.

1567
01:12:21,205 --> 01:12:23,840
GORGO, MORMO, YOU WANNA
HELP ME WITH THIS KNOT?

1568
01:12:27,277 --> 01:12:29,547
THIS IS THE WEIRDEST
BIG VALLEY EVER.

1569
01:12:31,448 --> 01:12:34,852
UH, WISH I BROUGHT A CHANGE
OF PANTS ON THIS TRIP.

1570
01:12:34,885 --> 01:12:38,822
THEY'RE ALL CRUNCHY.

1571
01:12:38,855 --> 01:12:40,457
WHAT IS KEEPING ME UP
TONIGHT?

1572
01:12:40,490 --> 01:12:41,992
I HAD A CUP OF TEA,
A TOUCH OF DINNER--

1573
01:12:42,025 --> 01:12:43,927
OH, RIGHT, GRANDMA
MUTILATED A COP.

1574
01:12:43,960 --> 01:12:45,562
THAT'D DO IT.

1575
01:12:50,200 --> 01:12:52,102
WELL, I'M GONNA GO
PUKE ON THE MAVERICK.

1576
01:12:55,605 --> 01:12:57,040
- AHH.
- OKAY, EVERYONE
HOLD IT A SECOND.

1577
01:12:57,073 --> 01:12:59,477
I JUST WANNA SEE
IF HE GETS HIS SHOES ON.

1578
01:12:59,510 --> 01:13:01,578
YE-- YES. YES.

1579
01:13:01,612 --> 01:13:03,047
GREAT. GLAD THEY
SHOWED THAT TO US.

1580
01:13:05,848 --> 01:13:07,717
GAH!

1581
01:13:07,752 --> 01:13:10,053
WHERE'D THEY FIND
THE 590-WATT LIGHT BULB?

1582
01:13:12,622 --> 01:13:14,390
I ACTUALLY NEED
SOMETHING MEAT-HOOKED.

1583
01:13:14,425 --> 01:13:16,260
I'M GONNA GO SEE
IF GRANDMA IS UP.

1584
01:13:19,930 --> 01:13:22,165
YEP, I THINK HE STILL HAS
THOSE SHOES ON, YOU GUYS.

1585
01:13:22,198 --> 01:13:23,900
I CAN HEAR THEM.

1586
01:13:23,933 --> 01:13:25,735
- I'M GONNA KEEP MY EYE
ON THE SITUATION.
- THANKS MIKE.

1587
01:13:25,768 --> 01:13:29,005
- I'LL LET YOU KNOW.
- GOOD, GOOD.

1588
01:13:29,038 --> 01:13:30,273
WELL, HEY, LOOK.

1589
01:13:30,307 --> 01:13:32,042
GRANNIES DO SWING
ON THE OUTHOUSE DOOR

1590
01:13:32,075 --> 01:13:33,743
WITHOUT THEIR NIGHTIES.

1591
01:13:37,380 --> 01:13:40,683
UH, HE'S GOT THE SHOES ON
HERE, THIS IS GOOD.

1592
01:13:40,717 --> 01:13:42,518
LITTLE BIT OF REDUNDANCY
ON THE SHOES IS GOOD, MIKE.

1593
01:13:42,552 --> 01:13:43,720
I'M GONNA
BACK YOU UP ON THIS.

1594
01:13:43,753 --> 01:13:45,822
THANKS.

1595
01:13:47,723 --> 01:13:49,125
YOU KNOW, UNLESS
THERE IS A CHANGE

1596
01:13:49,158 --> 01:13:50,860
I THINK WE CAN JUST ASSUME
HE'S WEARING THE SHOES

1597
01:13:50,893 --> 01:13:54,297
- FROM NOW ON.
- YEAH, YEAH, GOOD.

1598
01:13:54,330 --> 01:13:56,098
MAYBE THIS WAS
ONCE FAST-PACED,

1599
01:13:56,133 --> 01:13:57,835
AND SOMEONE SPILLED
A GRAPE NEHI ON IT,

1600
01:13:57,868 --> 01:13:59,637
AND IT GOT ALL GUMMY.

1601
01:13:59,670 --> 01:14:03,473
MAYBE.

1602
01:14:03,507 --> 01:14:05,642
I REALIZED WE HADN'T HAD
A STUTTERING CONVERSATION

1603
01:14:05,675 --> 01:14:09,145
FOR SEVERAL HOURS.

1604
01:14:09,178 --> 01:14:12,782
HE REJOICES
IN SPILLED BLOOD

1605
01:14:12,817 --> 01:14:14,183
AND THE BAYING OF DOGS.

1606
01:14:14,217 --> 01:14:16,653
MARILYN MANSON?

1607
01:14:16,687 --> 01:14:19,255
HE IS GORGO

1608
01:14:19,288 --> 01:14:20,357
AND MORMO.

1609
01:14:20,390 --> 01:14:24,427
♪ AND JOE ♪

1610
01:14:24,460 --> 01:14:27,130
IF YOU CAN HANG ON A SEC,
I'M ABOUT TO SAY SOMETHING.

1611
01:14:29,132 --> 01:14:31,133
JODIE,

1612
01:14:31,168 --> 01:14:34,370
YOU TURNED DOWN
THE ROAD YESTERDAY

1613
01:14:34,403 --> 01:14:36,773
BECAUSE YOU WANTED TO SEE
WHAT WAS UP THE OTHER END.

1614
01:14:36,807 --> 01:14:38,442
JUST LIKE THAT CHICKEN.

1615
01:14:38,475 --> 01:14:40,877
WELL, NOW YOU'VE SEEN IT.

1616
01:14:40,910 --> 01:14:44,047
BUT YOU WON'T BELIEVE IT.

1617
01:14:44,080 --> 01:14:46,148
I CAN'T.

1618
01:14:46,183 --> 01:14:49,687
- NOT CAN'T. WON'T.
- AH.

1619
01:14:49,720 --> 01:14:51,455
YOU WON'T BELIEVE
IN THE DEVIL

1620
01:14:51,488 --> 01:14:52,655
BECAUSE YOU'RE AFRAID

1621
01:14:52,688 --> 01:14:54,490
IF YOU BELIEVE IN HIM,
HE'LL BE REAL.

1622
01:14:54,525 --> 01:14:56,360
IT'S LIKE WHEN YOU WOULDN'T
BELIEVE IN PEANUT BUTTER.

1623
01:14:59,295 --> 01:15:02,332
HE IS REAL.

1624
01:15:02,365 --> 01:15:04,367
I HEARD HIM.

1625
01:15:04,400 --> 01:15:05,935
I FELT HIM INSIDE ME.

1626
01:15:05,968 --> 01:15:07,537
THAT WAS ACID REFLUX.

1627
01:15:07,570 --> 01:15:09,272
IT'S NOT TRUE.

1628
01:15:09,305 --> 01:15:12,375
FACE IT.

1629
01:15:12,408 --> 01:15:14,612
I'VE HAD TO.

1630
01:15:14,645 --> 01:15:16,247
DO YOU THINK I LIKE IT?

1631
01:15:16,280 --> 01:15:18,415
DO YOU THINK I'VE
ENJOYED ALL THESE YEARS

1632
01:15:18,448 --> 01:15:20,217
WITH THE DEVIL'S
SPIRIT INSIDE ME?

1633
01:15:20,250 --> 01:15:21,518
SURE, WE'VE HAD SOME LAUGHS.

1634
01:15:21,552 --> 01:15:23,020
IT HAPPENED, JODIE.

1635
01:15:23,053 --> 01:15:24,922
JUST LIKE IN YOUR DREAM.

1636
01:15:26,957 --> 01:15:30,060
THAT DREAM WAS COINCIDENCE.

1637
01:15:30,093 --> 01:15:31,562
IS IT A COINCIDENCE

1638
01:15:31,595 --> 01:15:34,097
THAT I KNOW THEY SANG
A HYMN IN YOUR DREAM?

1639
01:15:35,598 --> 01:15:36,900
THE GOOD CHRISTIANS

1640
01:15:36,933 --> 01:15:39,870
SANG A GOOD CHRISTIAN SONG

1641
01:15:39,903 --> 01:15:41,738
WHILE THEY WERE
BURNING MY SISTER.

1642
01:15:41,772 --> 01:15:43,840
AND THEY DIDN'T EVEN HAVE
A YOUTH HORN SECTION.

1643
01:15:49,847 --> 01:15:52,715
♪ AMAZING ♪

1644
01:15:52,748 --> 01:15:54,117
♪ GRACE-- ♪

1645
01:15:54,150 --> 01:15:56,487
♪ AND CHUCK ♪

1646
01:15:56,520 --> 01:15:58,955
♪ THE SOUND ♪

1647
01:15:58,988 --> 01:16:00,790
♪ THAT SAVED ♪

1648
01:16:00,823 --> 01:16:02,825
♪ A WRETCH-- ♪

1649
01:16:02,858 --> 01:16:05,695
♪ LIKE ME
PUBLIC DOMAIN ♪

1650
01:16:05,728 --> 01:16:07,863
♪ WE DON'T HAVE TO PAY ANYONE
HA-HA-HA-HA ♪

1651
01:16:09,667 --> 01:16:10,867
WHAT'RE YOU DOING TO ME?

1652
01:16:10,900 --> 01:16:12,768
♪ IT'S THAT WITCHCRAFT! ♪

1653
01:16:12,802 --> 01:16:15,438
♪ WICKED WITCHCRAFT ♪

1654
01:16:15,472 --> 01:16:16,707
WHY IS IT
SO IMPORTANT THAT

1655
01:16:16,740 --> 01:16:18,008
I BELIEVE IN THIS
DEVIL OF YOURS?

1656
01:16:18,042 --> 01:16:19,610
WELL, I GET A COMMISSION.

1657
01:16:19,643 --> 01:16:23,180
BECAUSE YOU CAN SAVE ME.

1658
01:16:23,213 --> 01:16:25,315
I'VE GOT A SICKNESS
IN ME, JODIE.

1659
01:16:25,348 --> 01:16:27,317
I'VE GOT OCCASIONAL
DEVIL WORSHIP.

1660
01:16:27,350 --> 01:16:29,485
YOU CAN FREE ME FROM IT.

1661
01:16:29,518 --> 01:16:32,322
BUT NOT UNLESS YOU
BELIEVE IT EXISTS.

1662
01:16:32,355 --> 01:16:34,290
AREN'T THERE ANY JESUITS
IN THE PHONE BOOK?

1663
01:16:34,323 --> 01:16:35,692
COME ON.

1664
01:16:39,997 --> 01:16:41,532
HOW CAN I HELP YOU?

1665
01:16:41,565 --> 01:16:43,700
WHAT CAN I,
A SINGLE PUSS, DO?

1666
01:16:47,503 --> 01:16:50,840
- BY BELIEVING WHAT
I'VE TOLD YOU--
- MM-HMM.

1667
01:16:50,873 --> 01:16:52,977
AND WHAT I'M GOING
TO TELL YOU.

1668
01:16:53,010 --> 01:16:56,178
LET ME PAUSE TO DRENCH
MY NEXT LINE IN MEANING.

1669
01:16:56,212 --> 01:16:57,480
I WANT TO HELP YOU.

1670
01:16:57,513 --> 01:17:01,183
BUT I'M REALLY BUSY
RIGHT NOW.

1671
01:17:01,217 --> 01:17:02,552
I LOVE YOU.

1672
01:17:02,585 --> 01:17:04,688
AND I'VE GROWN AWFULLY FOND
OF YOUR GRANDMA.

1673
01:17:08,758 --> 01:17:11,362
MAY I TOUCH YOUR SIDEBURN?

1674
01:17:11,395 --> 01:17:14,397
THEN HEAR THE REST OF IT.

1675
01:17:14,430 --> 01:17:15,598
I WANT TO HELP.

1676
01:17:15,632 --> 01:17:17,033
CONSARN IT, BREAK IT UP!

1677
01:17:17,067 --> 01:17:20,603
MY DAGNABBIT
CONTRACT WITH SATAN!

1678
01:17:20,637 --> 01:17:22,872
WOW, POOP DECK PAPPY

1679
01:17:22,905 --> 01:17:24,775
GETTING ALL UPSET HERE.

1680
01:17:24,808 --> 01:17:26,308
THEY TURNED ME DOWN
FOR THAT POLICY!

1681
01:17:26,343 --> 01:17:28,912
THEY SAID IT
COULDN'T HAPPEN!

1682
01:17:28,945 --> 01:17:32,248
[SERVO MUTTERS]

1683
01:17:32,282 --> 01:17:34,083
NO!

1684
01:17:34,117 --> 01:17:36,820
I TOLD YOU I COULD
TAKE YOU, YOU PANSIES!

1685
01:17:36,853 --> 01:17:38,122
I COULD TAKE
THE WHOLE FAMILY!

1686
01:17:38,155 --> 01:17:39,790
- WOW.
- [CROW CHUCKLES]

1687
01:17:46,963 --> 01:17:49,432
- WOW.
- CAN'T BELIEVE I HAVE
TO WASH SATAN'S TOWELS.

1688
01:17:55,038 --> 01:17:58,442
- MELISSA.
- CROSSROADS SEEM
TO COME AND GO.

1689
01:17:58,475 --> 01:18:01,243
IF ALL THIS WERE TRUE,

1690
01:18:01,277 --> 01:18:04,347
THAT WOULD MAKE YOU
127 YEARS OLD.

1691
01:18:06,248 --> 01:18:07,683
- YES.
- MAN, SHE'S GETTING

1692
01:18:07,717 --> 01:18:09,853
INTO STROM THURMOND COUNTRY.

1693
01:18:11,722 --> 01:18:14,190
[SERVO DOES TRAIN BELL]

1694
01:18:14,223 --> 01:18:17,327
IT'S THE TRAIN GOING
THROUGH THE PAUSE.

1695
01:18:17,360 --> 01:18:18,895
IS THIS STILL
THE SAME PAUSE,

1696
01:18:18,928 --> 01:18:20,663
OR IS IT TECHNICALLY
A SUB-PAUSE?

1697
01:18:20,697 --> 01:18:24,500
EVEN IF IT WERE TRUE,

1698
01:18:24,533 --> 01:18:26,202
I'D LOVE YOU ANYWAY.

1699
01:18:26,235 --> 01:18:27,837
I MEAN, I'D PUT YOU
IN A HOME, BUT...

1700
01:18:30,173 --> 01:18:31,742
UGH.

1701
01:18:36,112 --> 01:18:37,513
HEY, JOHN QUINCY ADAMS!

1702
01:18:37,547 --> 01:18:38,915
[GRANDMA SCREECHES]

1703
01:18:38,948 --> 01:18:40,683
- WOW.
- RUN, JODIE.

1704
01:18:40,717 --> 01:18:42,918
GRANDMA USED TO WORK
FOR THE L.A.P.D.

1705
01:18:42,952 --> 01:18:44,320
WITCH!

1706
01:18:44,353 --> 01:18:45,722
OH!

1707
01:18:48,092 --> 01:18:50,893
- OOPS.
- OH NO.

1708
01:18:50,927 --> 01:18:54,197
BURN, WITCH, BURN.

1709
01:18:54,230 --> 01:18:55,698
OH, AND GRANDMA HAD
JUST GOTTEN A JOB

1710
01:18:55,732 --> 01:18:58,768
AS A GREETER AT WAL-MART.

1711
01:18:58,802 --> 01:19:00,337
[DISTANT CROWD]
♪ AMAZING GRACE ♪

1712
01:19:00,370 --> 01:19:02,438
HEY, MIKE, WHAT WERE YOU GUYS
DOING DURING THE 70'S?

1713
01:19:02,472 --> 01:19:04,007
MAKING WITCH MOVIES?

1714
01:19:04,040 --> 01:19:06,543
INHALING HUGE CLOUDS
OF MARIJUANA?

1715
01:19:06,577 --> 01:19:09,512
BIG, UGLY FLARED PANTS ON?

1716
01:19:09,545 --> 01:19:11,347
WE HAD TO DO SOMETHING.

1717
01:19:11,380 --> 01:19:12,782
MELISSA, COME ON!

1718
01:19:12,815 --> 01:19:15,552
OH, SHE'LL BE FINE, COME ON.

1719
01:19:15,585 --> 01:19:16,720
[SONG CONTINUES]

1720
01:19:16,753 --> 01:19:18,020
I KNOW, WHEN
YOU'RE THAT AGE,

1721
01:19:18,053 --> 01:19:19,857
YOU'RE JUST READY
TO GO RIGHT UP.

1722
01:19:19,890 --> 01:19:21,357
THE SLIGHTEST SPARK
CAN GET IT GOING.

1723
01:19:21,390 --> 01:19:24,227
LET ME TELL YOU.

1724
01:19:24,260 --> 01:19:27,030
AW, NOW SHE'S MELISSA
"NO SHEDS" STRICKLAND.

1725
01:19:30,033 --> 01:19:31,433
MAN, NEVER LET EDIE SEDGWICK

1726
01:19:31,468 --> 01:19:33,903
BORROW YOUR LAKE CABIN.

1727
01:19:33,937 --> 01:19:36,005
I'VE DONE IT. NO GOOD.

1728
01:19:36,038 --> 01:19:38,408
LOOK AT IT GO, GRANDMA
MUST'VE EXPLODED OR SOMETHING.

1729
01:19:38,442 --> 01:19:41,578
MAN.

1730
01:19:41,612 --> 01:19:44,815
[SONG CONTINUES]

1731
01:19:44,848 --> 01:19:46,617
GRANDMA'S FLASH-PAPER
BATHROBE

1732
01:19:46,650 --> 01:19:48,985
TURNED OUT TO BE A MISTAKE.

1733
01:19:51,053 --> 01:19:52,655
OH, IF THE SEPTIC TANK
GOES UP,

1734
01:19:52,688 --> 01:19:54,657
WE'RE ALL IN TROUBLE.

1735
01:19:59,062 --> 01:20:00,363
IN THE WAKE OF THE TRAGEDY,

1736
01:20:00,397 --> 01:20:01,798
THE TOWN BUILT
A BETTER GRANDMA.

1737
01:20:01,832 --> 01:20:03,267
STRONGER,
WITH A STEEL FRAME,

1738
01:20:03,300 --> 01:20:04,968
AND A SPRINKLER SYSTEM.

1739
01:20:12,375 --> 01:20:14,443
NOW I JUST HAVE TO WATCH OUT
FOR MY OTHER GRANDMA.

1740
01:20:14,477 --> 01:20:17,313
SHE'S REALLY CRAZY.

1741
01:20:17,347 --> 01:20:19,815
MM-- UGH.

1742
01:20:19,850 --> 01:20:21,217
YOU THINK I WANTED
YOUR SALIVA?

1743
01:20:21,250 --> 01:20:24,187
IS THAT WHY YOU DID THAT?

1744
01:20:24,220 --> 01:20:26,355
HMM, NOT WORTH IT.
SORRY.

1745
01:20:26,388 --> 01:20:28,123
I HAD FUN, THOUGH.
SEE YA.

1746
01:20:31,360 --> 01:20:33,397
CAN YOU NOT FRENCH MY DAUGHTER
DURING BREAKFAST?

1747
01:20:33,430 --> 01:20:35,232
GOODBYE, SIR.

1748
01:20:35,265 --> 01:20:37,867
THANK YOU FOR TRUSTING ME.

1749
01:20:37,900 --> 01:20:39,068
I'LL KEEP MY WORD.

1750
01:20:39,102 --> 01:20:41,872
I'LL TELL NO ONE
OF YOUR BACKSWEAT PROBLEM.

1751
01:20:44,473 --> 01:20:46,208
WELL, LET'S LOCK YOU
BACK IN THE BARN.

1752
01:20:46,242 --> 01:20:48,345
I'LL WALK OUT
TO THE CAR WITH YOU.

1753
01:20:48,378 --> 01:20:50,113
COULD YOU DROP ME OFF
AT TANGLEWOOD?

1754
01:20:50,147 --> 01:20:52,648
I'M CONDUCTING MAHLER'S 10TH
THIS WEEKEND.

1755
01:20:57,320 --> 01:20:59,088
OPEN THE LENS MORE.
WE NEED MORE LIGHT!

1756
01:20:59,122 --> 01:21:01,023
MORE!

1757
01:21:01,057 --> 01:21:02,558
MM, I SEE GRANDMA
BEHIND THAT TREE.

1758
01:21:02,592 --> 01:21:04,593
YOU MIGHT WANNA
MAKE A RUN FOR IT.

1759
01:21:13,637 --> 01:21:15,138
I JUST WANTED TO ASK YOU,

1760
01:21:15,172 --> 01:21:16,640
WHILE WE'RE AWAY
FROM ALL THE OTHERS,

1761
01:21:16,673 --> 01:21:18,708
DO YOU THINK
WE'RE WEIRD AT ALL?

1762
01:21:18,742 --> 01:21:21,110
IT'S ALL TRUE, YOU KNOW,
EVERYTHING SHE TOLD YOU.

1763
01:21:21,143 --> 01:21:23,880
I'M SORRY, SIR,
I CAN'T BELIEVE THAT.

1764
01:21:23,913 --> 01:21:26,282
AND I CAN'T BELIEVE SHE'S
POSSESSED BY THE DEVIL, EITHER.

1765
01:21:26,315 --> 01:21:27,483
I SUPPOSE NOT.

1766
01:21:27,517 --> 01:21:28,918
WHATEVER.

1767
01:21:28,952 --> 01:21:31,320
BE CAREFUL.

1768
01:21:31,353 --> 01:21:32,922
GOODBYE, JODIE.

1769
01:21:32,955 --> 01:21:34,423
- GOODBYE, SIR.
- OH, AND, UH,

1770
01:21:34,457 --> 01:21:36,727
DON'T JOIN AL PACINO'S
LAW FIRM.

1771
01:21:39,963 --> 01:21:41,865
MAY THE DARK ONE HOLD
YOUR SOUL IN HIS CLUTCH--

1772
01:21:41,898 --> 01:21:45,802
I MEAN, UH, SAFE TRIP.

1773
01:21:45,835 --> 01:21:47,270
YO.

1774
01:21:47,303 --> 01:21:48,705
EH, NICE KID.

1775
01:21:48,738 --> 01:21:50,873
WELL, THE BOMB SHOULD GO OFF
IN A COUPLE OF MINUTES.

1776
01:21:53,577 --> 01:21:57,047
[SERVO HUMS ALONG]

1777
01:21:57,080 --> 01:21:58,282
AHH.

1778
01:21:58,315 --> 01:21:59,715
FRITZ KREISLER USED TO WEAR

1779
01:21:59,748 --> 01:22:01,517
A STRIPED SHIRT LIKE THAT.

1780
01:22:06,657 --> 01:22:09,258
SORRY, I GOT SO MANY
WALNUT HUSKS IN MY TEETH.

1781
01:22:13,830 --> 01:22:16,098
WELL, I SHOULD SAY GOODBYE
TO THE FISH, I SUPPOSE.

1782
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:19,768
WHERE THE HECK IS THAT
VILLAGE SMITHY?

1783
01:22:22,872 --> 01:22:24,340
[BOTS HUM, WHISTLE]

1784
01:22:24,373 --> 01:22:26,208
I AM HUNGRY,
BUT I CAN'T GO BACK

1785
01:22:26,242 --> 01:22:28,177
TO THE GROCERY STORE
AFTER THAT "ZAH" INCIDENT.

1786
01:22:30,780 --> 01:22:34,150
[SERVO HUMS]

1787
01:22:34,183 --> 01:22:35,485
WOW, LOOK AT THE SMOKE.

1788
01:22:35,518 --> 01:22:37,753
EVERYBODY MUST BE BURNING
THEIR GRANDMAS TODAY.

1789
01:22:41,257 --> 01:22:43,593
[SERVO HUMS ALONG]

1790
01:22:43,627 --> 01:22:46,562
HEY, I RAN OUT OF GAS.

1791
01:22:46,595 --> 01:22:49,132
I'M KIND OF A WOLF WHEN
I'M ALONE WITH MYSELF.

1792
01:22:49,165 --> 01:22:51,702
YEP.

1793
01:22:51,735 --> 01:22:53,737
HEY, THE ODOMETER'S
ALL SIXES.

1794
01:23:00,477 --> 01:23:02,812
WAIT A MINUTE,
WHERE'S MY IMMORTAL SOUL?

1795
01:23:02,845 --> 01:23:05,282
OH CRAP, I LEFT IT
BACK AT THE FARM.

1796
01:23:10,120 --> 01:23:11,620
WE'RE BACK AT THE BEGINNING.

1797
01:23:11,653 --> 01:23:13,790
THIS FILM IS
A MOBIUS STRIP.

1798
01:23:20,763 --> 01:23:22,165
MY FISH MOVED
AND DIDN'T LEAVE

1799
01:23:22,198 --> 01:23:23,800
A FORWARDING ADDRESS.

1800
01:23:27,203 --> 01:23:28,938
SEE, I DON'T GET
HOW THEY BILLED THIS

1801
01:23:28,972 --> 01:23:30,273
AS A "ROLLICKING MUSICAL."

1802
01:23:30,307 --> 01:23:33,175
NO.

1803
01:23:33,208 --> 01:23:35,712
THE ONLY KNOWN SHOTS
OF BIGFOOT IN A T-SHIRT.

1804
01:23:38,982 --> 01:23:40,417
COME, SIT IN THE CROTCH.

1805
01:23:40,450 --> 01:23:42,185
WELL-- YOU KNOW,
THE TREE...

1806
01:23:42,218 --> 01:23:46,222
RIGHT.

1807
01:23:46,255 --> 01:23:48,357
DRAW.

1808
01:23:48,392 --> 01:23:50,025
I LOVE YOU, MELISSA.

1809
01:23:50,060 --> 01:23:52,895
ALMOST AS MUCH AS I LOVE
WIDE-WHALE CORDUROYS.

1810
01:23:52,928 --> 01:23:55,365
IT DOESN'T MATTER THAT
THE DEVIL'S IN YOUR SOUL.

1811
01:23:55,398 --> 01:23:56,398
YEAH, LOOK FAMILIAR, MIKE?

1812
01:23:56,432 --> 01:23:57,900
YEAH-- HEY.

1813
01:23:57,933 --> 01:24:01,738
I LOVE YOU.

1814
01:24:01,772 --> 01:24:03,238
UH, ARE YOU BLOWING ME OFF,

1815
01:24:03,272 --> 01:24:04,907
OR IS THIS JUST
ONE OF OUR PAUSES?

1816
01:24:08,412 --> 01:24:10,947
OUR NEXT PAUSE
IS GONNA BE THIS BIG.

1817
01:24:15,418 --> 01:24:17,287
READY, WRESTLE!

1818
01:24:22,892 --> 01:24:24,260
THE DEVIL JUST HAPPENS TO BE

1819
01:24:24,293 --> 01:24:25,895
PEEKING OUT OF
HER MOUTH RIGHT NOW.

1820
01:24:25,928 --> 01:24:29,565
"HU--HEY!
GET OUT OF THERE!"

1821
01:24:29,598 --> 01:24:30,933
WELL, THEIR DATES ARE EASIER

1822
01:24:30,967 --> 01:24:32,802
WITHOUT GRANDMA
CLUBBING HIM TO DEATH.

1823
01:24:38,407 --> 01:24:40,210
HUH?

1824
01:24:40,243 --> 01:24:41,610
MAN, I THOUGHT
I WAS AN OPERATOR.

1825
01:24:41,643 --> 01:24:45,215
- HE'S FAST.
- WHOA.

1826
01:24:45,248 --> 01:24:46,748
YOU KNOW, MY MOM USED
TO HAVE A LITTLE SAYING.

1827
01:24:46,783 --> 01:24:48,250
IT'S JUST AS EASY
TO FALL IN LOVE

1828
01:24:48,283 --> 01:24:50,287
WITH A WOMAN WHO'S NOT
POSSESSED BY THE DEVIL.

1829
01:24:50,287 --> 01:24:53,590
MM-HMM.

1830
01:24:53,623 --> 01:24:55,592
I HAVE ONE CHEST HAIR.

1831
01:24:58,260 --> 01:25:00,597
OKAY, KIDS, THE PICNIC
IS THIS WAY, W-- AAH!

1832
01:25:00,630 --> 01:25:03,633
AAH!

1833
01:25:03,667 --> 01:25:05,935
YOU FREED ME.

1834
01:25:05,968 --> 01:25:07,570
I'VE TURNED INTO
GLORIA STUART AT LAST.

1835
01:25:07,603 --> 01:25:10,507
I LOVE YOU, MELISSA.

1836
01:25:10,540 --> 01:25:11,975
I DO LOVE YOU.

1837
01:25:12,008 --> 01:25:13,977
BUT WHY ARE YOU
SANDING MY SHOULDER?

1838
01:25:17,447 --> 01:25:20,350
YOU SEEM TO HAVE SOME SORT
OF TARP ON YOUR HAND.

1839
01:25:22,852 --> 01:25:25,255
YOU SEE, YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
TO EXPECT A LITTLE OF THIS

1840
01:25:25,288 --> 01:25:26,823
- WITH YOUR BRIDES OF SATAN.
- OH YEAH.

1841
01:25:26,857 --> 01:25:28,123
I SHOULD KNOW.

1842
01:25:28,157 --> 01:25:29,825
WHAT'S WRONG?

1843
01:25:29,858 --> 01:25:31,862
YOUR FACE.

1844
01:25:31,895 --> 01:25:33,597
WELL, WHAT'S WRONG
WITH MY FACE?

1845
01:25:33,630 --> 01:25:36,265
WELL, NOTHING, IF YOU
LIKE EUBIE BLAKE.

1846
01:25:36,298 --> 01:25:38,835
OH MY GOD.

1847
01:25:38,868 --> 01:25:40,437
I'VE BECOME
SIGOURNEY WEAVER.

1848
01:25:40,470 --> 01:25:42,172
HE CHEATED ME.

1849
01:25:45,040 --> 01:25:46,877
HE NEVER TOLD ME.

1850
01:25:46,910 --> 01:25:48,277
MAN, IF YOU CAN'T
TRUST THE DEVIL...

1851
01:25:48,310 --> 01:25:50,480
JODIE, I--

1852
01:25:50,513 --> 01:25:53,015
I'M GOING TO DIE.

1853
01:25:53,048 --> 01:25:56,385
- NO.
- YOU'RE 127 YEARS YOUNG.

1854
01:25:56,418 --> 01:25:57,820
THERE'S A WAY.

1855
01:25:57,853 --> 01:25:59,822
NO.

1856
01:25:59,855 --> 01:26:03,727
JODIE, NOT THAT WAY.

1857
01:26:03,760 --> 01:26:06,262
WHAT WOULD YOU HAVE OF ME?

1858
01:26:06,295 --> 01:26:08,665
DON'T LET HER DIE,
I LOVE HER.

1859
01:26:08,698 --> 01:26:10,200
OH BOY, NO I DON'T.

1860
01:26:10,233 --> 01:26:12,235
WILL YOU ACCEPT ME
AS YOUR MASTER?

1861
01:26:12,268 --> 01:26:14,203
YES.

1862
01:26:14,237 --> 01:26:17,173
NO. NO.

1863
01:26:17,207 --> 01:26:19,742
- THEN SAVE HER.
- MORLEY SAFER.

1864
01:26:19,775 --> 01:26:21,577
HIT HIM.

1865
01:26:21,610 --> 01:26:23,680
QUICKLY NOW, SAVE HER.

1866
01:26:23,713 --> 01:26:25,882
WELL, I GUESS THAT'S WHAT
I WAS CALLING YOU FOR, DEVIL.

1867
01:26:30,553 --> 01:26:32,422
UGH.

1868
01:26:32,455 --> 01:26:34,190
I SHOULD'VE ASKED
THE DEVIL TO THROW IN

1869
01:26:34,223 --> 01:26:36,558
SOME OTHER MODIFICATIONS
WHILE I WAS AT IT.

1870
01:26:42,832 --> 01:26:44,900
GOOD, SO WE'RE BOTH
IN THE CLUTCHES OF THE DEVIL

1871
01:26:44,933 --> 01:26:47,703
BECAUSE YOU WANTED SECONDS.

1872
01:26:47,737 --> 01:26:50,307
AND THEY DRIFT APART
AFTER THREE WEEKS.

1873
01:26:52,175 --> 01:26:53,777
UH, WE'RE GONNA HAVE
A LITTER OF JACKALS

1874
01:26:53,810 --> 01:26:55,578
IN NINE MONTHS, YOU KNOW.

1875
01:26:59,282 --> 01:27:02,485
THIS IS A GOOD PAUSE
WE'RE HAVING, HUH?

1876
01:27:02,518 --> 01:27:03,987
YOU KNOW, I'M GUESSING
THIS GUY'S GONNA BE

1877
01:27:04,020 --> 01:27:06,422
A FAIRLY MINOR SOLDIER
IN THE DEVIL'S ARMY.

1878
01:27:06,455 --> 01:27:07,857
PROBABLY HAVE A TINY PICTURE

1879
01:27:07,890 --> 01:27:10,360
- IN HELL'S NEWSLETTER.
- YEP.

1880
01:27:13,295 --> 01:27:14,830
THEY'D BETTER BOOK
A HALL IN HELL

1881
01:27:14,863 --> 01:27:15,965
FOR THEIR UNHOLY WEDDING.

1882
01:27:15,998 --> 01:27:19,835
IT'S LIKE A YEAR WAIT.

1883
01:27:19,868 --> 01:27:22,172
OH, I DON'T KNOW,
I DON'T TRUST THIS, MIKE.

1884
01:27:22,205 --> 01:27:23,973
I JUST THINK THIS
IS THE LONGEST PAUSE YET.

1885
01:27:24,007 --> 01:27:25,708
[MIKE CHUCKLES]

1886
01:27:28,043 --> 01:27:29,212
OKAY.

1887
01:27:29,245 --> 01:27:31,513
SO, IN THE END,
SATAN WINS, I GUESS.

1888
01:27:31,547 --> 01:27:34,217
YEP, PRETTY MUCH
A SHUT-OUT FOR SATAN.

1889
01:27:34,250 --> 01:27:35,485
YEP.

1890
01:27:35,518 --> 01:27:37,287
AAH, THE DEVIL!

1891
01:27:37,320 --> 01:27:39,155
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.

1892
01:27:39,188 --> 01:27:42,658
[MIKE MOANS]

1893
01:27:55,505 --> 01:27:56,905
SWEET DEAL.

1894
01:27:56,938 --> 01:27:58,040
HEY, HEY MIKE!

1895
01:27:58,073 --> 01:27:59,808
I JUST SOLD
MY SOUL TO SATAN.

1896
01:27:59,842 --> 01:28:01,410
OH, YOU DID?

1897
01:28:01,443 --> 01:28:03,045
SO I'M PROBABLY
GONNA HAVE LOTS

1898
01:28:03,078 --> 01:28:05,548
OF UNFATHOMABLE
WORLDLY POWER REAL SOON.

1899
01:28:05,582 --> 01:28:07,350
YEAH, I THOUGHT I'D GIVE YOU
THE HEADS-UP ON THAT.

1900
01:28:07,383 --> 01:28:09,052
OH, THAT'S REAL THOUGHTFUL
OF YOU, THANKS, CROW.

1901
01:28:09,085 --> 01:28:10,953
YEP, GOT A CONTRACT
RIGHT HERE.

1902
01:28:10,987 --> 01:28:12,788
FROM SATAN.

1903
01:28:12,822 --> 01:28:14,257
LET ME SEE THAT.

1904
01:28:14,290 --> 01:28:16,092
"SHALL TAKE POSSESSION
OF HIS MORTAL SOUL."

1905
01:28:16,125 --> 01:28:17,693
YEAH, THAT ALL SCANS.

1906
01:28:17,727 --> 01:28:19,595
OH, BUT LOOK AT THIS.
LITTLE MISTAKE HERE.

1907
01:28:19,628 --> 01:28:21,597
LOOKS LIKE YOU
SOLD YOUR SOUL TO STAN.

1908
01:28:21,630 --> 01:28:23,265
- NOT SATAN.
- HUH.

1909
01:28:23,298 --> 01:28:24,800
- YEAH.
- WELL, THERE'S
A NUMBER THERE.

1910
01:28:24,833 --> 01:28:26,702
- WOULD YOU MIND
CALLING IT, PLEASE?
- OH, YEAH. YEAH.

1911
01:28:26,735 --> 01:28:28,270
- WOW.
- YEAH, SEE, THIS--

1912
01:28:28,303 --> 01:28:30,473
THIS ISN'T EVEN
THE AREA CODE FOR HELL, SO--

1913
01:28:30,507 --> 01:28:32,408
- AH.
- YELLO? STAN JOHNSON.

1914
01:28:32,442 --> 01:28:33,642
AH, SEE, THERE YOU GO.

1915
01:28:33,677 --> 01:28:36,412
HI, STAN, THIS IS,
UH, MIKE NELSON.

1916
01:28:36,445 --> 01:28:39,315
- YOU'RE NOT BY ANY CHANCE
THE DEVIL, ARE YOU?
- UH, NOPE.

1917
01:28:39,348 --> 01:28:41,817
I'M A CPA AND INVESTMENT
CONSULTANT.

1918
01:28:41,850 --> 01:28:43,485
- DAMN.
- AH-HAH. YEAH.

1919
01:28:43,518 --> 01:28:46,155
HEY, I'M CALLING ON BEHALF
OF A CROW T. ROBOT.

1920
01:28:46,188 --> 01:28:48,758
OH, RIGHT.
LITTLE, SKINNY GOLD GUY?

1921
01:28:48,792 --> 01:28:50,158
KIND OF BUG-EYED? SURE.

1922
01:28:50,192 --> 01:28:52,728
YEAH, THAT'S THE GUY.
HEY, DID YOU BUY HIS SOUL?

1923
01:28:52,762 --> 01:28:54,397
YES, I DID.

1924
01:28:54,430 --> 01:28:56,765
I MANAGE A WELL-BALANCED
PORTFOLIO OF SOULS.

1925
01:28:56,798 --> 01:28:58,300
THEY CAN BE
VERY HIGH-YIELD.

1926
01:28:58,333 --> 01:29:00,603
UM-- UM, STAN, THIS IS CROW.

1927
01:29:00,637 --> 01:29:03,405
WHEN CAN I GET MY SOUL BACK?
IS THAT POSSIBLE?

1928
01:29:03,438 --> 01:29:05,575
OH, I'M SORRY, I RESOLD
YOUR SOUL ALREADY

1929
01:29:05,608 --> 01:29:07,677
TO CITYCORP IN
A BIG BLOCK OF SOULS.

1930
01:29:07,710 --> 01:29:09,112
UH, MAN, I AM GONNA
HAVE TO MAKE

1931
01:29:09,145 --> 01:29:11,713
SO MANY PHONE CALLS
TO GET MY SOUL BACK.

1932
01:29:11,747 --> 01:29:14,550
OH MAN-- OH, AND PEARL'S
BABYSITTER IS CALLING.

1933
01:29:15,918 --> 01:29:17,520
HELLO?

1934
01:29:17,553 --> 01:29:19,288
BE WITH YOU IN A MINUTE.

1935
01:29:19,322 --> 01:29:21,690
ALMOST FINISHED STORY TIME.

1936
01:29:21,723 --> 01:29:23,827
THEN EVERYONE GOES TO SLEEP.

1937
01:29:23,860 --> 01:29:25,828
UH, CAN I COME OUT NOW?

1938
01:29:25,862 --> 01:29:28,230
SHUSH, BAD DOG. GO TO SLEEP.

1939
01:29:28,263 --> 01:29:29,832
OKAY.

1940
01:29:29,865 --> 01:29:31,300
NOW, WHERE WAS I, BRIAN?

1941
01:29:31,333 --> 01:29:32,868
OH, UH,

1942
01:29:32,902 --> 01:29:35,838
THE TALL FELLOW
WAS REPEATEDLY REFUSING

1943
01:29:35,872 --> 01:29:38,975
TO INGEST
GREEN EGGS AND HAM.

1944
01:29:39,008 --> 01:29:40,877
THE SHORT FELLOW WAS

1945
01:29:40,910 --> 01:29:43,312
BIZARRELY INSISTENT UPON IT.

1946
01:29:43,345 --> 01:29:44,980
YES, VERY GOOD.

1947
01:29:45,013 --> 01:29:46,815
YEAH.

1948
01:29:46,848 --> 01:29:50,052
"I WILL NOT EAT THEM
IN A PLANE.

1949
01:29:50,085 --> 01:29:52,388
I WILL NOT EAT THEM
ON A TRAIN."

1950
01:29:52,422 --> 01:29:53,522
"ON A TRAIN."
RIGHT, YOU KNOW,

1951
01:29:53,555 --> 01:29:55,858
WHY DOESN'T HE JUST
LEAVE HIM ALONE?

1952
01:29:55,892 --> 01:29:58,493
HE HAS POINTEDLY
MADE HIS REFUSAL

1953
01:29:58,527 --> 01:30:00,162
TO EAT THIS DISH CLEAR.

1954
01:30:00,195 --> 01:30:02,030
THE MERE HYPOTHETICAL
CHANGING OF A LOCATION

1955
01:30:02,063 --> 01:30:04,000
IS IRRELEVANT AND TEDIOUS.

1956
01:30:04,033 --> 01:30:06,102
AND-- AND THAT SAM I AM

1957
01:30:06,135 --> 01:30:09,038
IS SO BLOODY REPETITIVE
I COULD SCREAM.

1958
01:30:09,072 --> 01:30:12,708
ARE WE A LITTLE
CRANKY, BRIAN?

1959
01:30:12,742 --> 01:30:15,545
NO, MADAM, I AM OVERTIRED.

1960
01:30:15,578 --> 01:30:17,113
SO I SHALL TURN IN NOW.

1961
01:30:17,147 --> 01:30:18,815
SO IF YOU WOULDN'T MIND,
PLEASE.

1962
01:30:18,848 --> 01:30:21,283
MY BLANKIE.

1963
01:30:21,317 --> 01:30:24,253
MY NOOKIE.

1964
01:30:24,287 --> 01:30:28,090
AND MY FRIEND.

1965
01:30:28,123 --> 01:30:30,627
OH. THANK YOU KINDLY.

1966
01:30:30,660 --> 01:30:34,163
GOOD MORROW TO YOU.

1967
01:30:34,197 --> 01:30:36,732
NIGHTY-NIGHT.

1968
01:30:36,765 --> 01:30:38,400
WELL, NOW, ME?

1969
01:30:38,433 --> 01:30:39,935
I'D DEFINITELY
EAT THEM ON A TRAIN.

1970
01:30:39,968 --> 01:30:41,570
QUIET, NO BARK.

1971
01:30:41,603 --> 01:30:43,338
--DELICIOUS ON A TRAIN,
BUT A PLANE?

1972
01:30:43,372 --> 01:30:45,007
I'D HAVE TO THINK
ABOUT A PLANE.

1973
01:30:45,040 --> 01:30:47,310
MAYBE SUBSTITUTE
BACON FOR HAM.

1974
01:30:47,343 --> 01:30:48,677
THAT SOUNDS KIND OF NICE,
AND WE COULD HAVE A--

1975
01:30:48,710 --> 01:30:50,012
OH-- OH BOY.

1976
01:30:50,045 --> 01:30:51,780
[BOBO CHIRPS]

1977
01:30:51,813 --> 01:30:52,748
- NO BARK.
- [THUMPS]

1978
01:30:52,782 --> 01:30:54,350
OW! I'M NOT BARKING.

1979
01:30:54,383 --> 01:30:55,752
I WAS JUST TALKING-- OW!

1980
01:30:55,785 --> 01:30:57,353
I'M COMMENTING ON THE STORY.

1981
01:30:57,387 --> 01:30:58,787
THERE'S NO BARKING
INVOLVED AT ALL.

1982
01:30:58,822 --> 01:31:00,255
- NO, NO BARK.
- [THUMP]

1983
01:31:00,288 --> 01:31:02,458
OW! NO, I'M NOT SURE
YOU SEE MY POINT.

1984
01:31:02,492 --> 01:31:04,327
HERE, IT'S LIKE THIS.
RATHER THAN BARKING,

1985
01:31:04,360 --> 01:31:05,795
AS YOU ASSUMED,
I WAS ACTUALLY--

1986
01:31:05,828 --> 01:31:07,597
- [THUMP]
- OH, COME ON!

1987
01:31:07,630 --> 01:31:08,998
...TALKING, I'M-- OW!

1988
01:31:09,032 --> 01:31:10,800
- NO!
- OW!
- NO BARK.

1989
01:31:10,833 --> 01:31:12,968
OW! I'M NOT BARKING,
I'M-- OW!

1990
01:31:13,002 --> 01:31:15,137
- BAD DOG.
- [BOBO MUMBLES]

1991
01:31:15,170 --> 01:31:17,138
- JEEZ! OW-- OW!
- BAD DOG.

1992
01:31:17,173 --> 01:31:18,875
OW! STOP IT!

1993
01:31:56,245 --> 01:31:58,313
THIS IS WHERE
THE FISH LIVES.
